{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element","id":1463010,"title":"The Disparate Alliance is a Bad Setting Element","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-07T11:25:27-07:00","id":1463010,"title":"The Disparate Alliance is a Bad Setting Element","content":"Continued from the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5/page25\">earlier thread</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's <i>already</i> a faction for anti-statist traditionalist mages who want to preserve the old ways and keep their brand of magic alive in modern times. It's called the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The Disparates basically seem like inserts to give minority cultures their own faction. Even leaving aside the incongruity in the Dreamspeakers still belonging to the Traditions and the Knights Templar belonging to the Disparates (???), the four factions are meant to cover some really big ideas. The Traditions are the classic wizards keeping myth and wonder alive in a secular age. The Technocracy is the cold and sterile science relentlessly driving that secular age. The Nephandi are existence-hating nihilists who've given up on building a better world. The Marauders are mad wizards who've been shattered by hubris, trauma, and tragedy. Again, these factions cover big ideas that can encompass a wide range of belief systems and sociopolitical ideologies. The Traditions and the Technocracy can be left wing or right wing. They are bigger than that. They represent timeless ideas that were just as relevant in 1992 as they are in 2021.<br /> <br /> And then we have the Disparates. They don't encompass a timeless idea that feels like it could've existed in 1992. They feel pulled from 2010s+ Twitter woke culture that insists on greater representation for groups that were represented just fine in the existing four factions. And, on top, there are some author lines that say they're the best at fighting the Nephandi and better/more hardcore than the Traditions in various ways. They feel like an obvious author favorite and clumsy insert to make the game more culturally sensitive.<br /> <br /> I say this as someone who's pretty politically left-leaning.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, another reason I don't like the Disparates? They don't gel as neatly with the game's metaphysics.<br /> <br /> The Marauders are Dynamism. The Technocracy is Stasis. The Nephandi are Entropy. The Traditions are Balance. The factions represent each branch of the Metaphysic Trinity* (or the union of those branches) and the four types of Avatars. There's good symmetry there. It feels right from a game design and an in-universe perspective.<br /> <br /> The Disparates align with... what branch of the Trinity? I guess Balance too, but that makes them redundant. We already have a faction that covers Balance. It's just another way the new faction feels awkwardly tacked on.<br /> <br /> * It also raises interesting questions--the Marauders and Nephandi are obviously screwed up and can't be allowed to win the Ascension War, so does that mean the Technocracy is too, because any mage society aligning too closely with one Trinity branch is a bad idea? Or, is Stasis actually the only &quot;good&quot; branch? That'd mean Traditions are tainted for their association with Dynamism and Entropy, but less so than the Marauders and Nephandi because they still have some Stasis as a stabilizing influence. This is a fun debate mages can have and the Disparates just muddy the waters, because the Trinity is no longer clearly linked to the main factions in the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462986#post1462986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, to me, the Disparates all seem like they're highly traditional, natural xenophobes with an unwillingness to share or be subject to outside power and thus they want outsiders to fuck off.<br /> <br /> Why the fuck would such people make an alliance when the whole point was they don't want a fucking alliance? Strikes me as yuppie, virtue signalling bullshit of the highest order.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462992#post1462992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do mages really work so well together globally that locals can't fend them off? They're not vampires who can send wave after wave of neonates at the problem till it goes away. Mages are hard to replace and nodes need to be defended. The Wu Lung, for example; Canonically sexist, very probably racist. But the fact that they're threatened by outsiders gives them very good reason to work together well, <i>with other Wu Lung</i>. How many other disparates have a presence in China? What use is a knights templar in shanghai? And why would a KT come to China to help with matters when he has more pressing issues back home? The two big-dogs are also less inclined to bother the Wu Lung when they're dancing with eachother.<br /> <br /> Anyhow we're wildly off topic.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I always thought the Wu Lung and Ngoma worked just fine in the Order of Hermes. Some of the Crafts work fine as outsiders, but I thought Revised had a good idea moving more of them into the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461282-my-review-of-sabbat-the-black-hand-4-5-5?p=1462996#post1462996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was also the perfect antidote to the various bad racial stereotypes by saying \u201cthere\u2019s more styles of magical practice in Asia than just mystic martial arts; not every magician on the continent of Africa is some tribal Shaman.\u201d It\u2019s acknowledging the practitioners as individuals and not just racial stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Frankly, instead of the Disparate Alliance (the crafts of which had mostly joined the Traditions in Rev), I think a far better approach would have been, sorta like Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, a look at how the principles of each Tradition can be found around the world (ex. just about every culture has some variation of the cycle of life and death the Euthanatos/Chakravati harness in their practices).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. If you stick more Crafts in the Traditions, they become more multicultural. I think some work okay staying independent Crafts, because they are just so isolated or intolerant they aren't interested in alliances, but some of them work great in the Traditions.<br /> <br /> I also don't have an inherent problem with Western mages having more power in mage society. Western civilization has, for much of modern history, dominated the world and it makes sense that would carry over to some degree.<br /> <br /> Obviously, there are factors in mage society that don't make it a complete analogue. Senex is an African archmage who's probably the most personally powerful figure left in the Traditions, if one assumes the fall of Doissetep is canon.<br /> <br /> But it feels like the Disparate Alliance was expressly designed to give minority cultures more power in the setting for contrived reasons. I think the setting is more compelling when mages from minority cultures <i>are</i> angry about about having less power/representation in the Traditions. (And even more so in the Technocracy.) I generally prefer not fixing real-world injustices in fictional settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T11:40:30-07:00","id":1463012,"title":"","content":"I've always assumed the Traditions were meant to be a global alliance of people feeling oppressed by Western imperialism and economic pressures. Then again, I've always been somewhat uncomfortable with the Technocracy being treated as a progressive organization.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the new Star Wars EU making the head of the Empire after Palpatine into a gay black woman.<br /> <br /> I feel like it undermines them as a totalitarian authoritarian regime of conformity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T11:51:43-07:00","id":1463016,"title":"","content":"I thought that was stupid too. The old EU had the Empire as an expressly sexist and xenophobic institution. Women and aliens were discriminated against.<br /> <br /> Because they're the bad guys.<br /> <br /> It's just more stupid virtue signaling. Who cares about everything that's wrong with Disney as a company? We get more strong minority characters!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T11:56:45-07:00","id":1463017,"title":"","content":"I can't comment on the motives of Disney and it may have just been, &quot;Let's make fascism harder for Far Right individuals to co-opt like they've been doing.&quot; It is weird that the most prominent person of color they could make in the setting's heirarchy would be the head of the fascists, though.<br /> <br /> That's off topic, though.<br /> <br /> I don't hate the idea of the Disparate Alliance but I note that given the Knights Templar are members, they could easily have gone the other way and make it the &quot;crazy intolerant mages.&quot;<br /> <br /> Imagine if the anti-vaxxers were unaccepted by the Traditions and went there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T12:45:51-07:00","id":1463023,"title":"","content":"My main problems with the Disparate Alliance are...<br /> <br /> A) How can an alliance of Xenophobics work? <br /> <br /> And B) If they've been downtrodden and oppressed for five hundred years, what the hell do they have for resources? <br /> <br /> I could see the Hollows Ones trying to build alliances with these groups, but not their being successful. Take the Alibatin, they presume all other Mages are slack fools and easy dupes of the Nephandi. How could the Hollow Ones get the Alibatin to treat them with respect when neither the far better organized Hermetic Order nor the profoundly pious Celestial Chorus never achieved that? The Hollow Ones would look like helpless kittens to the Alibatin.<br /> <br /> The Ngoma and the Children of Knowledge would be friendly, but weary. I can't see the Bata'a, the Sisters of Hypolita, the Templars, the Taftani, or the Wu Lung even speaking to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T12:47:40-07:00","id":1463024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463012#post1463012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always assumed the Traditions were meant to be a global alliance of people feeling oppressed by Western imperialism and economic pressures. Then again, I've always been somewhat uncomfortable with the Technocracy being treated as a progressive organization.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the new Star Wars EU making the head of the Empire after Palpatine into a gay black woman.<br /> <br /> I feel like it undermines them as a totalitarian authoritarian regime of conformity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Traditions are a political and military alliance, they have agreed rules, ranks etc, it is very loose, but it is there, so having a 'just leave us alone' faction forming makes sense, it happened in the cold war as well, with the Non-Aligned movement it really depends how organised the Disparates.really are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T13:01:58-07:00","id":1463025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element#post1463010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you stick more Crafts in the Traditions, they become more multicultural.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you reboot the setting with the Crafts as existing and long standing parts of the Traditions with political power, the Traditions become more multicultural.<br /> <br /> When you stick them in via metaplot, they become 2nd and 3rd class citizens as there's only nine seats on the Council and the Crafts would either have to accept joining a Tradition at the bottom, or not have a representative on the Council.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't have an inherent problem with Western mages having more power in mage society. Western civilization has, for much of modern history, dominated the world and it makes sense that would carry over to some degree. </div> </div> </div>But this inherently comes with the alienation of mages that became a lot of the Crafts; esp. the ones that were once part of the Traditions or were offered a place in them.<br /> <br /> When the Traditions were founded <b>half</b> of the mages recruited for the Dreamspeakrs told the European dominated Council to screw off.<br /> <br /> The big point of the Crafts was to highlight how the Council's norms and procedures were harming some of its ideals by scaring off potential allies via the Western-centric nature of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it feels like the Disparate Alliance was expressly designed to give minority cultures more power in the setting for contrived reasons. </div> </div> </div>How is, &quot;minority cultures that don't want to bend to the Tradition's liberal melting pot, but still want the power to fend off the Technocracy, gathering together in a mutual defense pact,&quot; giving them significantly more power in the setting, or contrived?<br /> <br /> As I said in the other thread, the Alliance makes sense as a product of the metaplot: the Traditions, at their best point in opening up their ranks to the more amenable Crafts instead did the opposite, and the Technocracy was still being the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the setting is more compelling when mages from minority cultures <i>are</i> angry about about having less power/representation in the Traditions. </div> </div> </div>That's still the case with or without the Disparate Alliance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I generally prefer not fixing real-world injustices in fictional settings. </div> </div> </div>What real-world injustice has been fixed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463012#post1463012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, I've always been somewhat uncomfortable with the Technocracy being treated as a progressive organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're not progressive. But sometimes progressive politics and the Union's goals line up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sort of like the new Star Wars EU making the head of the Empire after Palpatine into a gay black woman. </div> </div> </div>I know we're trying to move off this, but I hate how revisionist Star Wars stuff has become.<br /> <br /> Have we forgotten the two big contenders to take over the Empire after Palpatine and Vader died in Legacy EU? Director Isard (a woman) and Grand Admiral Thrawn (an alien).<br /> <br /> In the old EU, and the new canon, Star Wars has always had the position that the Battle of Endor led the remaining Empire to become more open to people they'd formerly kept out of power taking charge because they took too big of a loss to disregard loyal talent. The new canon just changed the details of who got to the top.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T13:18:49-07:00","id":1463026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463025#post1463025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know we're trying to move off this, but I hate how revisionist Star Wars stuff has become.<br /> <br /> Have we forgotten the two big contenders to take over the Empire after Palpatine and Vader died in Legacy EU? Director Isard (a woman) and Grand Admiral Thrawn (an alien).<br /> <br /> In the old EU, and the new canon, Star Wars has always had the position that the Battle of Endor led the remaining Empire to become more open to people they'd formerly kept out of power taking charge because they took too big of a loss to disregard loyal talent. The new canon just changed the details of who got to the top.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that's a weird thing to bring up when both Timothy Zahn and Michael A. Stackpole made it clear in the books that Isard and Thrawn faced huge amounts of discrimination in their rise to power, so much so that Isard only became leader of Intelligence by executing her own father while Thrawn was exiled to the Unknown Regions.<br /> <br /> And the Old EU had that as the result of Admiral Daala who executed all of the previous Imperial leaders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T13:19:59-07:00","id":1463027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463023#post1463023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) How can an alliance of Xenophobics work?</div> </div> </div> </div>The core five members of the Alliance aren't xenophobes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And B) If they've been downtrodden and oppressed for five hundred years, what the hell do they have for resources? </div> </div> </div>As M20 specifically addresses, one of the unifying factors for many of the members of the Alliance is that they've gotten very good at hiding their resources from the Traditions and Technocracy, because it's easier for them to let the big factions think they're diminished into insignificance. They've spent a long time gathering resources because they've been doing it while trying to avoid being seen doing so (including making tentative contacts with each other more recently).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take the Alibatin, they presume all other Mages are slack fools and easy dupes of the Nephandi. </div> </div> </div>The Batini are literally one of the core groups actively trying to make the Alliance happen because they need more allies to fight the Nephandi. They''re doing a lot of the outreach here. They were founding members of the Traditions because they want this sort of thing to work, but the Traditions were a failure in their eyes. The Alliance is they next stab at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How could the Hollow Ones get the Alibatin to treat them with respect when neither the far better organized Hermetic Order nor the profoundly pious Celestial Chorus never achieved that? </div> </div> </div>Easily? The Batini care about unity. The Hollow Ones rejecting the false unity of the Traditions and seeing the potential for the true Unity of the Alliance is all the Batini need. You seem to be vastly exaggerating the Batini's feelings about other mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't see the Bata'a, .. even speaking to them. </div> </div> </div>Why? The Bata'a and the Hollowers have a lot in common as people disrespected by the Traditions for not being &quot;proper&quot; mages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T13:34:12-07:00","id":1463029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463026#post1463026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like that's a weird thing to bring up when both Timothy Zahn and Michael A. Stackpole made it clear in the books that Isard and Thrawn faced huge amounts of discrimination in their rise to power, so much so that Isard only became leader of Intelligence by executing her own father while Thrawn was exiled to the Unknown Regions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not weird when you realize the Sloane's rise to power is basically a mirror of Thrawn's? She was probably going nowhere until she managed to impress Palpatine and Vader, who never cared about the whole &quot;white human men&quot; bias thing outside of using it as a tool for control, who then protected and guided her career as a valued true believer in the Sith imperial cause.<br /> <br /> Her creator's specifically stated that one of the things he wanted to put into the stories with her that he felt was missing, was that the Empire lacked idealist true believers in the original films. The Moffs and Admirals were all portrayed as more political opportunists wanting power, even though fascist movements need a wave of true believers as well. Sloane was meant to add a true believer. She'd never get forced choked by Vader for mocking the Force, or failing to fanatically uphold the Empire's goals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T15:13:14-07:00","id":1463031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463025#post1463025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I As I said in the other thread, the Alliance makes sense as a product of the metaplot: the Traditions, at their best point in opening up their ranks to the more amenable Crafts instead did the opposite, and the Technocracy was still being the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the metaplot isn't my cup of tea, so that's moot for me. The setting as presented in 2e got along fine without a Disparate Alliance and was more thematically coherent for it.<br /> <br /> I like some of the Crafts being parts of the Traditions all along, mainly because it opens more options for players. I like other Crafts joining later, but probably before the '90s, and some being sufficiently isolated and/or xenophobic to remain independent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have we forgotten the two big contenders to take over the Empire after Palpatine and Vader died in Legacy EU? Director Isard (a woman) and Grand Admiral Thrawn (an alien). </div> </div> </div>Thrawn and Isard both only checked one diversity box. Alien (probably straight) man, white (probably straight) woman. Gay black woman checked three. Four if you include her naturally long and Afro-textured hair.<br /> <br /> The virtue signaling is strong in this one.<br /> <br /> Thrawn and Isard were written as minorities because (I'm partly speculating here) the writers thought if they rose to the top anyway in minority-unfriendly institutions, that was a solid way of establishing their badass-itude. I'm pretty sure Sloane was written to check as many diversity boxes as possible, which is fairly consistent with the state of Disney Star Wars these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 10-07-2021, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T15:57:23-07:00","id":1463033,"title":"","content":"I think the Disparate Alliance has the potential to fill a much needed role in the Earthly setting. When you have two factions like the Traditions and the Technocracy facing each other in opposition, neither is going to care that much about what view their enemy has of them. It is like two people facing each other in hand to hand combat fought to the death with no witnesses. If one can win by the most underhanded tactic imaginable, there is no reputational cost to consider. In a Power Triangle, the conflict is going to be more interesting. <br /> <br /> While Book of the Fallen (which I mostly enjoyed) presents the option of making the Nephandi a very present and Earthly threat, there are considerations a storyteller has to make. Given what you know about the past experiences of your players, IRL, how much do you want to rely on a villain group whose themes are brutality, abuse, child abuse, sadism and &quot;fail a saving throw, lose your soul&quot; - the Caul? Given what you <i>Don't</i> know about player past experience... same question. My answer is: very little and later on, when they have enough experience as players to deal with such themes. So, for the important foundational chapters of my story, I need a third Earthly faction, if only as a mental reference to explain why the Traditions and Technocracy don't engage in a full on war without worry of how their actions reflect on them on the &quot;World Stage&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, I have some of the same difficulties with the Disparate Alliance that others described upstream. Luckily, there is an easier way to approach this than trying to map the relationships between Alliance members. There are three questions that could help any storyteller in planning to include the Disparate Alliance:<br /> <br /> 1) Given a vast geographic area, like Africa, that the Disparate Alliance is supposed to be dominant in, what fun possibilities can you you explore that are pertinent to that part of the world?<br /> <br /> 2) Can you imagine <i>A Single NPC</i> who is from one of the Crafts belonging to the Disparate Alliance that you would enjoy running in your Chronicle? Looking at it this way takes some of the pressure off that would come with calculating the politics of a DA Cabal.<br /> <br /> 3) Is there a Plot that you can run with this NPC that would not be possible with the other factions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T20:19:47-07:00","id":1463048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463031#post1463031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The virtue signaling is strong in this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your insistence in arguing &quot;virtue signalling&quot; as the beginning and end and only possible reason behind everything you don't like in those takes is annoying. What is even the problem if that was true? This is merely an <i>Ad Hominem</i> that tries to attack both the authors and anyone siding with them while trying to delegitimize any real perception of problems before they are even stated.<br /> <br /> First of all, arguing the Disparate Alliance without considering the Metaplot is ridiculous, you're arguing that they're a bad addition to the story because they don't gel with your headcanon that ignores this same story. What is even the point!? The books have a metaplot, it wasn't as strong all the time but was there since day 1, and the canon lore is this metaplot. You can use the books without it, but you can't expect to have a meaningful conversation with others based on your use instead of on the book that everyone read.<br /> <br /> Second, <b>you</b> may not have a problem with the game presenting &quot;western&quot; Mages not only as holding the power, but also the Mages from other cultures either accepting that or doing nothing, so they can uphold your fancy metaphysics. But other people may have a right to disagree without being called names. Europe, US and Russia became really powerful in the last centuries, but we at the rest of the world weren't just taking sides or digging holes. There are associations and alliances all around the world between countries and/or non-government entities to hold on their own against the most powerful, some of them pretty similar to the DA in some aspects, as the Global Governance Group.<br /> <br /> If the setting existed in a form where the Traditions could represent every culture in an equal footing, it would make sense. But this isn't the setting we have. If the setting had the war in such a state that Crafts simply couldn't exist outside the Traditions without being obliterated, it would make sense, but this is also far darker than what we actually have. The setting we have always had disgruntled Crafts that didn't wanted to bow to the Council. With reason, because this same setting also always had the Traditions still having many structures that aren't so open to interpretation as you describe. Not only the Council as a whole have a strict power structure, the component Traditions too have theirs and are entitled to force newcomers into their own ways.<br /> <br /> Another problem is that sometimes there are real problems behind the &quot;virtue signaling&quot; decisions you don't like. The Get of Fenris had a camp of Nazis, which just make sense. But irl there were countless LARPs and tables where real Neo-Nazis hid behind the excuse of playing their characters to harass everyone else. This was a real problem that had to be dealt with. The same happens in Star Wars, where the portrayal of the Empire also attracted a lot of white supremacist fans that get real angry if you spell it out that the Empire IS white supremacist, &quot;because they don't want the franchise tainted by politics&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mage is a game played the world around by all sorts of people, not only by WASP dudes. Presenting the player's culture as subsumed by European structures and incapable of standing on its own even after Awakening is a pretty shitty message, <u><b>especially for a setting that was political since day 1 of its first release and stay openly political to date</b></u>. You want to ignore other cultures fighting for self-advocacy and uniting for mutual protection because it harms your metaphysics? Sure, your table, do away with the DA. But don't use shitty arguments to invalidate others' opinions and make your headcanon seem as more valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T21:55:34-07:00","id":1463056,"title":"","content":"I wish I could upvote Monteparnas more, because WOW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T22:15:07-07:00","id":1463057,"title":"","content":"As I've said, I think Disparates can stand up on their own.<br /> <br /> Mage is essentially about the battle of ideas, so a homefield advantage is <i>huge. </i>If the Local culture brings more people into your craft, and it also makes your magic less vulgar than your rivals, you are just going to be in a strong place.<br /> <br /> Another issue with the Disparate alliance is that, well, mages don't really want to deal with people from other crafts. Mages covet natural resources and create technology that only they can use. Trade? Well that Gris Gris is useless for you, and how are you going to get the prime out of that battery when you're a Daoist scholar-mage ? OK, it might not be that bad, but remember you're dealing with a lot of proud, racist xenephobes and a lot of them will think of their practice as holy and thus won't be too keen on having their holy sites and holy objects molested by &quot;allies&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let's take the Wu Lung again.<br /> Your conflict with the Akashics is more about... resources than anything else. Yeah, sure, you want to promote yourself over them so you get more recruits. Locally speaking there's little reason for them to be doing much better than you, and they're a lot less unified than you owing to their size.<br /> Your conflict with the technocracy is more serious, but to them the Akashics are a more threatening enemy and there to take more of the brunt for you. The Technocracy has a decisive cultural disadvantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T23:09:48-07:00","id":1463060,"title":"","content":"The issue with the Disparates mostly boils down to missing context, and any explanation that is given in M20 core is severely lacking.I can understand having an IC justification to have multi-Craft PC cabals, since that was kind of an issue with the Crafts before M20. But the explanation given is...kind of messy.<br /> <br /> (Although even then, Rev's choice of &quot;the Crafts were destroyed and the survivors were absorbed into the Traditions&quot; has offensive implications.)<br /> <br /> Well, we'll see what the &quot;Lore of the Crafts/Disparates&quot; book that's being attached to the &quot;Lore of the Traditions&quot; KS ends up delivering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463012#post1463012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, I've always been somewhat uncomfortable with the Technocracy being treated as a progressive organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm uncomfortable with the Traditions being treated as a progressive organization because...it's in their name. &quot;Traditions&quot;. Does that sound like the title of an ultra progressive group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T23:49:56-07:00","id":1463065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject off Virtue Signaling, it is a real phenomenon. One of it's more problematic features is that it is competitive. It puts pressure on everyone to participate and can become ridiculous. Here is an example of what virtue signaling might sound like after an echo chamber has ramped everyone inside up to max:<br /> <br /> &quot;People who don't put diversity in their Chronicles are total Nazis that aren't worth consideration as human. I, on the other hand, love to use the opportunity my players give me to introduce them to diverse characters from all over the world whose cultures it has been my pleasure to study in depth before putting a single pencil mark on an NPC character sheet. And, of course, I emphasize the unique and amazing things diverse characters bring to the story, which is written to serve the purpose of reminding people of their unearned privilege (you know I'm looking at you, straight white dinosaur).&quot;<br /> <br /> QUOTE=monteparnas;n1463048]You want to ignore other cultures fighting for self-advocacy and uniting for mutual protection because it harms your metaphysics? Sure, your table, do away with the DA.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are to continue exploring the DA (which I seriously want to do), the reverse of this would be: Include, in your story, other cultures fighting for self-advocacy and uniting for mutual protection with flexible and expanded Paradigms suitable to their perspective AND your Chronicle. I would also add: When their inclusion in the story makes sense.<br /> <br /> Here are some IRL examples that come to mind:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E8Qsr2UrdoY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E8Qsr2UrdoY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E8Qsr2UrdoY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E8Qsr2UrdoY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpjxElfNpks\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpjxElfNpks\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpjxElfNpks\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zpjxElfNpks </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Once again, I throw down this challenge. Can anyone think of a concept for a Single DA character that would be fun for a storyteller to use as an NPC ally or rival to the PCs? - Rather than debating encyclopedic knowledge of a faction viewed from a distance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Solificati coroner who helps investigate/cover up weird goings on, Ahl-i-Batin arbitrator called in to keep the crafts/Traditions from clashing to badly, Knight Templar: basically Michael Carpenter from the Dresden Files, call then in to apply large amounts of holy beat stick, and as moral guide who legit is trying to live the nicer parts of the new testament. Sisters of Hippolyta 'transporter' works for an underground railroad, helping people awakened or not, escape war zones, drug wars, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T00:35:43-07:00","id":1463067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463031#post1463031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the metaplot isn't my cup of tea, so that's moot for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't have too much to add to monteparnas's point on this. But if you can't even analyze the Disparates in the context that they're presented, what point can you make?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Disparate Alliance is bad setting element because I ignore the setting elements that matter to their narrative,&quot; is a meaningless argument to make. You don't have to like the metaplot to judge the Alliance on what's actually presented in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like some of the Crafts being parts of the Traditions all along, mainly because it opens more options for players. I like other Crafts joining later, but probably before the '90s, and some being sufficiently isolated and/or xenophobic to remain independent. </div> </div> </div>This is more an argument that the Traditions flawed in their execution (they have no place for the Crafts to occupy that doesn't make the Crafts social inferiors) than it has anything to do with the Disparate Alliance as a setting element.<br /> <br /> It would have also ruined the narrative of the Hollow Ones back in 2e for things to be this way. Part of the whole point of the Hollowers was that they were valuable enough allies to the Traditions that the Traditions could have really used them to fully join the organization, but the Traditions' politics didn't give the Hollowers a place of their own among the Traditions; and the Hollowers didn't want to get shoved into one of the existing Traditions and lose what made them different. That tension was an essential part of the most prominent Craft in the game for three editions, and it wouldn't work if the Traditions had carved out a way to include the Crafts already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thrawn and Isard both only checked one diversity box. </div> </div> </div>Please point me to the place where there's a clearly defined theory on how a number of demographic/descriptive &quot;boxes checked&quot; is a thorough literary analytical technique. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The virtue signaling is strong in this one. </div> </div> </div>While I generally agree with why &quot;virtue signaling&quot; is meaningless buzzwords...<br /> <br /> You know what's true? <b>Virtue signaling is the core of Star Wars narratives</b>. Seriously. That's my whole point here. There's this insipid trend in criticism of the modern day Star Wars franchise that seems completely blind to what Star Wars was when it started. &quot;The Empire is all old white men, and the Rebels are diverse and multicultural&quot; is baked into the first movie. That's virtue signaling! White men bad! Diversity good! Women in positions of power good! The original trilogy bash you over the head with this repeatedly.<br /> <br /> If you don't like virtue signaling, you don't like Star Wars, because Star Wars has always been moralizing about these things since Luke's last name was Starkiller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure Sloane was written to check as many diversity boxes as possible, which is fairly consistent with the state of Disney Star Wars these days. </div> </div> </div>1) Are you saying John Jackson Miller is a liar, since he's Sloane's creator and he's stated what went into her creation publicly (and it's not what you're saying)?<br /> <br /> 2) Are you aware that John Jackson Miller was writing Star Wars EU material before Disney bought the franchise?<br /> <br /> 3) Have even read A New Dawn to see what Sloane is like as a character when she was first introduced?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463057#post1463057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another issue with the Disparate alliance is that, well, mages don't really want to deal with people from other crafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to who? The Crafts are noted as being suspicious of outsiders as a generality, and isolationists by necessity, but very few of them are written such that they have no interest in other mages. They just don't like the terms other mages tend to want to interact with them on.<br /> <br /> Which is, of course, the appeal the Alliance makes to its members. They get to decide how they contribute. No Council that forces a specific ruling body on them, or requires they start conforming to adapt to each other's methods and styles. Just an agreement of mutual defense and shared intelligence on their enemies is required of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages covet natural resources and create technology that only they can use. </div> </div> </div>The Disparate Alliance, since it's made up of Crafts that have made a lot of compromises in the name of survival, have quite a large number of member organizations that are rather adaptable. The Bata'a, Children of Knowledge, and Hollowers especially are all hard to keep from being able to use &quot;stuff only we can use&quot; with the sheer diversity of styles each of them contains.<br /> <br /> But the Alliance is a trade organization, it's a military reaction to the Ascension War refusing to stay away from people that don't want to be part of it, and the growing power of the Nephandi as the Traditions and Technocracy keep fighting each other. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's take the Wu Lung again. </div> </div> </div>Why? They're not one of the core five Crafts that started the Alliance. They're portrayed as one of the least bought into the whole enterprise.<br /> <br /> And you don't even touch on the explicit reason they joined: the Nephandi. The Wu Lung are one of the Crafts who only joined once the pitch got around to sharing information on Nephandi activities and help stopping them (and the Nephandi don't give a shit about traditional cultural borders, so having allies that can ambush a yacht with a Nephandus on it that escaped from Shanghai into the Polynesian islands is very useful).<br /> <br /> ---------------------------<br /> <br /> Also, in general, people keep tossing around the term &quot;xenophobic&quot; or some variation of that.<br /> <br /> None of the core Disparates are openly xenophobic; and there's barely much of a case for being closeted xenophobes. Even the Wu Lung who are Chinese supremacists, don't actually fear other cultures (and also they care about Chinese ethnicity, not country of origin, so they're not going to be hostile to Chinese Americans); they're way to prideful for that.<br /> <br /> Most of them have strong baked in prejudices, and many of them take that to bigotry on some level, but that's not inherently xenophobia; and thus isn't going to inherently stop them from joining an alliance. European colonialists were openly bigoted towards Native Americans, and that didn't stop there from being lots of alliances of tribes and colonies vs. other tribes and other colonies. Common enemies make for strange bed fellows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T01:10:17-07:00","id":1463069,"title":"","content":"Point of order but in the OG star wars movie, the rebels looked like this<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://starwarz.com/tbone/wp-content/uploads/2011/08/85.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> That's a lot of white human males. Alongside a single black man I think they get two alien pilots in <i>The Empire Strikes Back</i>. All those aliens, as Obi Wan puts it, belong in a &quot;Hive of Scum and Villainy&quot;. GL might've made a good point of female leaders, but there's not much else there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T01:20:23-07:00","id":1463070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject off Virtue Signaling, it is a real phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general concept might be real, but humans have also been doing it for all of recorded history. I can easily cite biblical passages condemning people that care more about performing for the public instead of holding to actual beliefs.<br /> <br /> The Internet use of the phrase is just a thought-terminating cliche at this point. It's a label used to end analysis and discussion by impugning something as &quot;bad&quot; without actually having to demonstrate that it is so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can anyone think of a concept for a Single DA character that would be fun for a storyteller to use as an NPC ally or rival to the PCs? - Rather than debating encyclopedic knowledge of a faction viewed from a distance. </div> </div> </div>A Hollower information broker that specializes in knowledge of other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> A cross-Craft cabal of a Templar, Taftani, and a Batini working to help clean up the utter supernatural mess that is the canon state of Cairo while preserving Egypt's diverse culture in the post-Arab Spring environment.<br /> <br /> A Wu Lung investment banker that's using the Belt and Road Initiative to take control over land in east Africa (of the ideas off the top of my head this one is the easiest to do as ally or rival)<br /> <br /> A Sister of Hippolyta that goes into abusive homes to get women and children out and to shelters even if it risks pissing off physically dangerous or well connected people that could bring trouble to other mages by association.<br /> <br /> The Kopa Loei that keeps asking Pele to ruin road construction to protect sacred lands, but has been getting to blatant about it and it's starting to get unwelcome attention on all levels... from the new curse highway tourist craze, to the Technocrats getting tired of their projects being behind schedule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T01:30:46-07:00","id":1463071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463069#post1463069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order but in the OG star wars movie, the rebels looked like this</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, now do the RotJ briefing. The one with multiple people of color, multiple women, and a bunch of aliens that aren't Chewy and were never in Mos Eisley... but also Chewy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T01:50:01-07:00","id":1463072,"title":"","content":"Putting &quot;Virtue Signaling&quot; aside, the Disparates don't really add diversity. Even the most seemingly West-centric Trad are shown to be multicultural. The Hermetics are shown to have had members from multiple different cultures all held together by their mystic focus on High Ritual. The Dreamspeakers and Verbena have members in every culture on the planet. We were shown Sons of Ether who were Native Brazilians from the Amazon rainforest. On the contrary, it's the Disparates who have single culture groups. An Hermetic can be a scholar from anywhere. A member of the Ali Batini has to be an Arab or at least from the Arab influenced cultural area that runs from Morocco to Pakistan (yes I know they don't all speak Arabic, I focused on Arab cultural influence on a profound level). That one European, who totally immersed himself in Arab culture was accepted was a big deal. The Wu Lung are explicitly and proudly racist. Even groups like the Ngoma and the Polynesian group (whose name I can't spell) while not bigoted don't accept actual outsiders. Contrast that with both the Traditions and the Union who proudly embrace all Humanity. The Union may be dangerous fools but they understand racism is evil. <br /> <br /> In the end, the Disparates aren't a group that can achieve cohesion. Only a few of the groups like the Children of Knowledge and the Ngoma get the value of alliance with others. Most, like the Ali Batini and the Wu Lung, can only see value of using others. Or like the Hollow Ones, the Sisters of Hypolita, and the Taftani, they simply wish to shout at others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-08-2021, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T02:05:46-07:00","id":1463073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463012#post1463012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always assumed the Traditions were meant to be a global alliance of people feeling oppressed by Western imperialism and economic pressures. Then again, I've always been somewhat uncomfortable with the Technocracy being treated as a progressive organization.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the new Star Wars EU making the head of the Empire after Palpatine into a gay black woman.<br /> <br /> I feel like it undermines them as a totalitarian authoritarian regime of conformity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Traditions are the people who want to obliterate technology and return the world to...depends on which tradition tbh, but some earlier time with crappy medicine and worse human rights is the usual answer, sure the Awakened will be casting fireball and teleporting, but the average peasant will be dying of cholera or the plague (if the Order of Hermes, Akashics or Verbena win) or living in a smoky Victorian slum (Sons of Ether), or in a weird anarcho-capitalist cyberpunk land if the Virtual Adepts . Like the traditions aren't nice, and they aren't progressive, the tend to be less bad than the Conventions, and are certainly less bad than the Nephandi or Marauders, but this is still the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463072#post1463072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting &quot;Virtue Signaling&quot; aside, the Disparates don't really add diversity. Even the most seemingly West-centric Trade are shown to be multicultural. The Hermetics are shown to have had members from multiple different cultures all held together by their mystic focus on High Ritual. The Dreamspeakers and Verbena have members in every culture on the planet. We were shown Sons of Ether who were Native Brazilians from the Amazon rainforest. On the contrary, it's the Disparates who have single culture groups. An Hermetic can be a scholar from anywhere. A member of the Ali Batini has to be an Arab or at least from the Arab influenced cultural area that runs from Morocco to Pakistan (yes I know they don't all speak Arabic, I focused on Arab cultural influence on a profound level). That one European, who totally immersed himself in Arab culture was accepted was a big deal. The Wu Lung are explicitly and proudly racist. Even groups like the Ngoma and the Polynesian group (whose name I can't spell) while not bigoted don't accept actual outsiders. Contrast that with both the Traditions and the Union who proudly embrace all Humanity. The Union may be dangerous fools but they understand racism is evil.<br /> <br /> In the end, the Disparates aren't a group that can achieve cohesion. Only a few of the groups like the Children of Knowledge and the Ngoma get the value of alliance with others. Most, like the Ali Batini and the Wu Lung, can only see value of using others. Or like the Hollow Ones, the Sisters of Hypolita, and the Taftani, they simply wish to shout at others.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Traditions allow a certain amount of variation, as long as it stays in it's lane and shuts up, look how they treated the Hollow Ones for an example, and look at who leads the traditions, the leadership tends to be old white Europeans (Except the Euthanatoi and Akashics) , and the 'variety' allowed is 'ideas that are 95% the same as ours. willing to submit to our commands and be our cannon fodder' Again the Traditions aren't a social club, they are more like Operation Gladio with funny robes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-08-2021, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T02:57:32-07:00","id":1463074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463048#post1463048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your insistence in arguing &quot;virtue signalling&quot; as the beginning and end and only possible reason behind everything you don't like in those takes is annoying. What is even the problem if that was true? This is merely an <i>Ad Hominem</i> that tries to attack both the authors and anyone siding with them while trying to delegitimize any real perception of problems before they are even stated.<br /> <br /> First of all, arguing the Disparate Alliance without considering the Metaplot is ridiculous, you're arguing that they're a bad addition to the story because they don't gel with your headcanon that ignores this same story. What is even the point!? The books have a metaplot, it wasn't as strong all the time but was there since day 1, and the canon lore is this metaplot. You can use the books without it, but you can't expect to have a meaningful conversation with others based on your use instead of on the book that everyone read.<br /> <br /> Second, <b>you</b> may not have a problem with the game presenting &quot;western&quot; Mages not only as holding the power, but also the Mages from other cultures either accepting that or doing nothing, so they can uphold your fancy metaphysics. But other people may have a right to disagree without being called names. Europe, US and Russia became really powerful in the last centuries, but we at the rest of the world weren't just taking sides or digging holes. There are associations and alliances all around the world between countries and/or non-government entities to hold on their own against the most powerful, some of them pretty similar to the DA in some aspects, as the Global Governance Group.<br /> <br /> If the setting existed in a form where the Traditions could represent every culture in an equal footing, it would make sense. But this isn't the setting we have. If the setting had the war in such a state that Crafts simply couldn't exist outside the Traditions without being obliterated, it would make sense, but this is also far darker than what we actually have. The setting we have always had disgruntled Crafts that didn't wanted to bow to the Council. With reason, because this same setting also always had the Traditions still having many structures that aren't so open to interpretation as you describe. Not only the Council as a whole have a strict power structure, the component Traditions too have theirs and are entitled to force newcomers into their own ways.<br /> <br /> Another problem is that sometimes there are real problems behind the &quot;virtue signaling&quot; decisions you don't like. The Get of Fenris had a camp of Nazis, which just make sense. But irl there were countless LARPs and tables where real Neo-Nazis hid behind the excuse of playing their characters to harass everyone else. This was a real problem that had to be dealt with. The same happens in Star Wars, where the portrayal of the Empire also attracted a lot of white supremacist fans that get real angry if you spell it out that the Empire IS white supremacist, &quot;because they don't want the franchise tainted by politics&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mage is a game played the world around by all sorts of people, not only by WASP dudes. Presenting the player's culture as subsumed by European structures and incapable of standing on its own even after Awakening is a pretty shitty message, <u><b>especially for a setting that was political since day 1 of its first release and stay openly political to date</b></u>. You want to ignore other cultures fighting for self-advocacy and uniting for mutual protection because it harms your metaphysics? Sure, your table, do away with the DA. But don't use shitty arguments to invalidate others' opinions and make your headcanon seem as more valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to write up something about the original post but this hits the nail on the head.<br /> <br /> I would also add that the idea the Crafts are an &quot;obvious author favourite&quot; is heavily undermined by the fact that M20 presents them decently neutrally. Metaplot options include the Disparate Crafts being 100% incorrect about the whole Nephandi thing, or their belief that the Technocracy and Traditions are run by Nephandi might actually be a Nephandic plot! &quot;Isn't paranoia fun.&quot; The book is upfront about their good and bad sides. We're shown that they stand up for downtrodden and ignored aspects of Magick which didn't fit into the Hermes and Merlin Club, but we're also shown that every group coming to the table brings some arguably regressive and xenophobic ideas with them. They feel like a decently realistic setting element given their common cause, and the fact that their common cause is one of the few things they have in common sounds like a source of... interesting conflict?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T03:11:08-07:00","id":1463075,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Due to the controversial nature of virtue signalling, despite the existence of performative progressiveness being a real academic issue debated by academics, I'd prefer if we avoid accusations of that and kept to the debate of their in-and-out-of-universe game merit.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T03:19:37-07:00","id":1463078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463073#post1463073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions are the people who want to obliterate technology and return the world to...depends on which tradition tbh,</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't. Like, the point of the Traditions working together is that they don't want to impose their paradigms on the world, leaving it up to people to determine for themselves. Like, some of the characters in-setting kinda believe what you're saying; especially the Technocrats, but it's pretty explicitly not true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T03:20:24-07:00","id":1463079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463048#post1463048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is even the problem if that was true?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because in my experience, the more aggressively authors push a social agenda, the worse their stories and worldbuilding in their settings tends to be. Such authors also tend to disrespect the works of authors that have come before them.<br /> <br /> Sloane isn't even the only Star Wars example. The recent comics also give us Han Solo's ex-wife Sana Starros, another black LGBT woman. We get a story with her where she sidelines Lando Calrissian (a straight black man), makes him look like a chump, and the writers plays it for laughs. Lando is treated with disrespect so that Sana looks cooler.<br /> <br /> Lando is an iconic character with decades of history and fan goodwill. When he suffers setbacks, he needs to be treated with respect. Darth Vader does the exact same thing to Lando in ESB--sidelines him, makes him look like a chump, and even gets in lots of iconic lines (&quot;I am altering the deal&quot;) at his expense. But nothing is played for laughs about it. We feel the tough position Lando is in, and when he later defies the Empire and leads the attack on the Death Star II, it's a powerful series of moments that reinforce the OT's themes of redemption and hope. Lando is treated with dignity by the writers even when he is humiliated in the story. His humiliation drives the story and furthers its themes. That's good writing.<br /> <br /> Lando in the comics is treated as a joke for no apparent purpose except enabling a more diverse character to score points at his expense. This happens all the time in media these days; an established character within a franchise is treated with disrespect so that a newer and more diverse character can look cool at their predecessor's expense. This happens because the authors want to show that diverse characters have primacy in their settings.<br /> <br /> When handled well, greater diversity in stories should not be a problem. There's no reason that Lando couldn't have been an LGBT black woman in the context of the OT's story. (Whether Lucas could have found another actor with Billy Dee Williams' charm and charisma is debatable.) Lando's race, gender, and sexuality aren't important to his character. Hell, Darth Vader could even have been a queer black woman if the writers explained how she was ignorant of her childrens' existences.<br /> <br /> Too often instead, diversity is not handled well. Authors aggressively push a social message to show how woke they are, do so at the expense of established settings and characters, and deliver a worse story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, arguing the Disparate Alliance without considering the Metaplot is ridiculous, you're arguing that they're a bad addition to the story because they don't gel with your headcanon that ignores this same story. What is even the point!? </div> </div> </div>M20 respects people who choose not to use metaplot. My &quot;headcanon&quot; is supported by the book. Almost every metaplot development gets its own Future Fates sidebar saying this is optional and suggests a number of ways GMs can utilize the metaplot development in question, including not using at all.<br /> <br /> Except for the Disparate Alliance. There is no sidebar saying they are optional. Even if you are playing in a setting with 2e metaplot, the book's stance is that the Disparate Alliance is an essential component of Mage's setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages not only as holding the power, but also the Mages from other cultures either accepting that or doing nothing, so they can uphold your fancy metaphysics. </div> </div> </div>My &quot;fancy metaphysics&quot; are the axis around which the setting turns. Why does the Council specifically have Nine Traditions? Why don't they seek to become the Ten, Eleven, or Even More Than Eleven Traditions, since more friends are good? Because of the Nine Spheres. Because symbolism and &quot;fancy metaphysics&quot; hold literal power in Mage's setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the setting existed in a form where the Traditions could represent every culture in an equal footing, it would make sense. But this isn't the setting we have. </div> </div> </div>We have whatever setting we choose to play with at our tables. A stance that M20 directly supports, with the sole exception of the Disparate Alliance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Get of Fenris had a camp of Nazis, which just make sense. But irl there were countless LARPs and tables where real Neo-Nazis hid behind the excuse of playing their characters to harass everyone else. This was a real problem that had to be dealt with. </div> </div> </div>The way you deal with this problem is by not playing with Nazis. VtM doesn't have any explicitly Nazi factions for vampires, but I still once had a prospective player for a VtM game pitch a Nazi PC. He came up with that character concept just fine on his own. (Turning him down from the game was an easy decision.)<br /> <br /> Racists will be racists and assholes will be assholes regardless of the PC options available to them. Game books have no power to legislate player behavior. Bad people, Nazis and otherwise, will always be attracted to good games. You cannot keep them out from the hobby except at your own table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same happens in Star Wars, where the portrayal of the Empire also attracted a lot of white supremacist fans that get real angry if you spell it out that the Empire IS white supremacist, &quot;because they don't want the franchise tainted by politics&quot;. </div> </div> </div>And so instead fascism gets championed by queer black women. I guess you've lost the racists, and the fascists can instead say, &quot;The Empire isn't a fascist institution. Look how culturally progressive it is.&quot; Maybe more people will think the Empire aren't such bad guys after all when queer black women can rise to its top-most echelons.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they won't, because people's sociopolitical views are unlikely to be significantly moved by Star Wars, and writers should just focus on writing good stories. Writing inferior stories with the aim of advancing a real-world sociopolitical agenda is tainting the franchise with politics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You want to ignore other cultures fighting for self-advocacy and uniting for mutual protection because it harms your metaphysics? </div> </div> </div>As has been pointed out, GMs who want a more culturally inclusive Nine Traditions can incorporate more of the Crafts into them. The more Crafts that are incorporated, and the earlier they are incorporated, the more culturally diverse the Traditions become. GMs who prefer a more European-dominated Traditions can also use the game's 2e setting where the Disparate Alliance doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage is a game played the world around by all sorts of people, not only by WASP dudes. </div> </div> </div>I should know, considering I'm not one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 10-08-2021, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T05:02:29-07:00","id":1463085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463067#post1463067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't have too much to add to monteparnas's point on this. But if you can't even analyze the Disparates in the context that they're presented, what point can you make?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Disparate Alliance is bad setting element because I ignore the setting elements that matter to their narrative,&quot; is a meaningless argument to make. You don't have to like the metaplot to judge the Alliance on what's actually presented in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>The context they are presented says the Disparate Alliance exists even in a setting where all metaplot developments are optional. The text outside of the Future Fates sidebars doesn't mention any metaplot. It says the Disparates formed in the '90s, but that it. Nothing about the Avatar Storm, the fall of Doissetep and Horizon, or the Ascension Warrior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would have also ruined the narrative of the Hollow Ones back in 2e for things to be this way. Part of the whole point of the Hollowers was that they were valuable enough allies to the Traditions that the Traditions could have really used them to fully join the organization, but the Traditions' politics didn't give the Hollowers a place of their own among the Traditions; and the Hollowers didn't want to get shoved into one of the existing Traditions and lose what made them different. That tension was an essential part of the most prominent Craft in the game for three editions, and it wouldn't work if the Traditions had carved out a way to include the Crafts already. </div> </div> </div>Or the Traditions treated the Hollow Ones poorly because they didn't take many of them seriously as mages (<i>&quot;Just rebellious angry Goth kids&quot;</i>), the nine seats on the Council were already filled, and they wanted the Hollow Ones to just join other Traditions rather than stay together as their own. When the Crafts in Revised joined the Council, they became camps in the most similar Traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's this insipid trend in criticism of the modern day Star Wars franchise that seems completely blind to what Star Wars was when it started. &quot;The Empire is all old white men, and the Rebels are diverse and multicultural&quot; is baked into the first movie. That's virtue signaling! White men bad! Diversity good! Women in positions of power good! The original trilogy bash you over the head with this repeatedly. </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/a/a0/Victory_Celebration_ANH.png/revision/latest?cb=20121227220043\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Leaving aside how there are almost exclusively white men here, and the wookiee never gets a medal...<br /> <br /> The OT doesn't bash you over the head with anything. Whether Mon Mothma is a white man or Palpatine is a black woman is immaterial to their roles in the story. If the writers had an agenda, it's impossible to tell, because RotJ is still a good story even if you change the characters' genders and races around.<br /> <br /> With characters like Rey? Disney's agenda is very easy to tell, and the character's bad writing and Mary Sue qualities are justified in the name of delivering a strong female character and feminist icon to a modern audience.<br /> <br /> The sequels would still be bad movies if Rey's character was made male, so the actual diversity isn't the problem. It's the fact that writers who are most vocal about including greater diversity in stories usually deliver bad stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T05:15:20-07:00","id":1463087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463072#post1463072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A member of the Ali Batini has to be an Arab or at least from the Arab influenced cultural area that runs from Morocco to Pakistan (yes I know they don't all speak Arabic, I focused on Arab cultural influence on a profound level).</div> </div> </div> </div>This hasn't been the case for the Batini in centuries. While those recruited into the Craft have to go to said area for training, the Batini are one of the few truly global Crafts (and have been since Revised, that's not a M20 change). As noted in Lost Paths, they adapt their cultural trappings to their location... they're the Subtle Ones after all. They don't conduct their business in Arabic if it's not a local language.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even groups like the Ngoma and the Polynesian group (whose name I can't spell) while not bigoted don't accept actual outsiders. </div> </div> </div>The Ngoma consider most of a continent of 1.3 billion people &quot;insiders&quot; in this regard, as well as the diaspora of African peoples around the world.<br /> <br /> The Kopa Loei have far less people to draw on, but still have dozens of cultures that are in their own in-group.<br /> <br /> I don't disagree with the idea that the Crafts moving into the Traditions would be a big helping of multiculturalism for the Council, but it's important not to sell the Disparates short here too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end, the Disparates aren't a group that can achieve cohesion. </div> </div> </div>That's up for debate, or rather, up for exploration. One of the central conflicts of the faction is how tenuous their current cooperative spirit is, and how to resolve that without violating their founding principle of not infringing on each member Craft's internal affairs. The book is pretty clear that it's possible they could find a path to cohesion... even if it's just out of familiarity as the other mage factions aren't going anywhere anytime soon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most, like the Ali Batini and the Wu Lung, can only see value of using others. Or like the Hollow Ones, the Sisters of Hypolita, and the Taftani, they simply wish to shout at others. </div> </div> </div>Huh? The Batini literally value unity above all else. They joined the Traditions because they wanted it to be what it was idealized to be, but left because the reality wasn't close. They want to find a way to get mages to coexist and cooperate towards the goal of mutual respect.<br /> <br /> The majority of the current Alliance members are presented as seeing the value in the enterprise, even if high skeptical that it will work. Like... where are you getting this stuff? The Hollowers aren't generally shouty, the Sisters don't waste their time yelling about their beliefs and spend most of their time living in small isolated communities, and even the Taftani have adapted to the 21st century with a new approach to their ways in M20.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463073#post1463073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions are the people who want to obliterate technology...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... I guess it's officially a true Mage thread now.<br /> <br /> Again, no this isn't true. The early Traditions might have wanted this. The modern Traditions want something different. We know what it looks like: Horizon.<br /> <br /> Horizon still had a major class issue between mages and the unawakened, but it was a realm where hypertech cellphones worked along side healing prayers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463079#post1463079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 respects people who choose not to use metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 respects people that don't want to use the end of 2e and into Revised metaplot. All of the 1e and early to mid-2e metaplot is assumed to have happened in the text. None of the 20th books is truly metaplot agnostic, they roll the metaplot back a bit and then don't move it forward in a significant way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except for the Disparate Alliance. There is no sidebar saying they are optional. </div> </div> </div>There's a sidebar that says that it's a completely probably outcome of the combination of some of the members of the Crafts joining the Traditions and the Disparate Alliance to just end up with the Disparate Alliance joining the Traditions fully.<br /> <br /> So, yes the Alliance isn't &quot;optional&quot; in the sense that the book assumes it happens, but it gives you a path to take the faction completely off the table.<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance just falling apart back into it's component Crafts because it doesn't work out is also completely a valid option of what to do with it.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to include them in your games... nothing breaks because they're brand new and barely functional as it is.<br /> <br /> And besides stating your dislike of them being presumed to be part of the setting, you still haven't really addressed the issue of the thread's title: are they a bad setting element even if you don't like the metaplot that provides the context of their formation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My &quot;fancy metaphysics&quot; are the axis around which the setting turns. </div> </div> </div>Odd. The setting held up fine the all of these groups were independent Crafts. Modern day Mage has always had more than four groups of mages. The setting also turned just fine back before the Order of Reason went full on &quot;we represent Stasis!&quot; and were still radical dissidents in the times when everyone was a mystic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why does the Council specifically have Nine Traditions? </div> </div> </div>The Hermetics demanded it, even though it cost them multiple groups that would have otherwise joined, because they wanted nine seats on the Council more than caring about appeal to other groups wanting to be treated as equals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because symbolism and &quot;fancy metaphysics&quot; hold literal power in Mage's setting. </div> </div> </div>Please name one thing in the setting that actually would metaphysically change if the Council had seven seats? Or eighteen? Or forty nine? Or eight one? Numerology has lots of options besides nine that have significant meaning. Squares are also a big deal (9x9 would be more significant to a Kabbalist than 9x2, even if 18 is still an important number).<br /> <br /> Technically the Council has 10 seats anyway, but the 10th is symbolically unoccupied.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way you deal with this problem is by not playing with Nazis. </div> </div> </div>The way you deal with the problem is both.<br /> <br /> Gaming books shouldn't make it look like it's acceptable to espouse Nazi ideology via the character faction options, and groups need to be careful to weed out problematic people.<br /> <br /> RPG books set the tone for the game, so yes, the authors have a responsibility for setting a tone in this regard too. It doesn't magically fix the world, but it makes it easier for the people playing to keep Nazis out of their games by making it harder for them to sneak in with concepts that are just using the options in the books. It's not about stopping Nazis from being who they are, but about making it easier for the rest of us to spot them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And so instead fascism gets championed by queer black women. </div> </div> </div>Again... have you actually read the books with Sloane in them? Because you have a very strange fixation on the surface level of the character and don't, at all, seem interested in actually bringing up examples from the text to show she's a bad character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The Empire isn't a fascist institution. Look how culturally progressive it is.&quot; Maybe more people will think the Empire aren't such bad guys after all when queer black women can rise to its top-most echelons. </div> </div> </div>Which they did with Thrawn back in the day, because they're not arguing in good faith about it. The main real world historical examples of fascism are heavily linked to racism, gender role enforcement, and conservative Christian views on sexuality, those are products the time and place, not the underlying psychology and ideology. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Writing inferior stories with the aim of advancing a real-world sociopolitical agenda is tainting the franchise with politics. </div> </div> </div>This is very amusing considering how horrible of a writer George Lucas is,and how much he relied on using Western political messaging to cover up cribbing Japanese cinema to come up with the original stories.<br /> <br /> Again, what always frustrates me with all of this is how utterly political Star Wars has always been. Is there bad writing in Star Wars? Sure. Always has been (see: Lucas). The best Star Wars stories are always overtly political. Lots of the bad stories are overtly political too. Makes you think maybe the problem isn't writing political stuff... but that some of the authors just aren't good fits for Star Wars.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T06:05:12-07:00","id":1463088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463085#post1463085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The context they are presented says the Disparate Alliance exists even in a setting where all metaplot developments are optional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides above post?<br /> <br /> That's not context. You know it's OK to say, &quot;The Disparate Alliance isn't something I like or intent to use, but it works in the game if you do.&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't have to create a Gordian Knot of fallacies to justify a preference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or the Traditions treated the Hollow Ones poorly because they didn't take many of them seriously as mages (<i>&quot;Just rebellious angry Goth kids&quot;</i>), the nine seats on the Council were already filled, and they wanted the Hollow Ones to just join other Traditions rather than stay together as their own. </div> </div> </div>And some of the Traditions were ready to give up the ceremonial tenth seat to them too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Leaving aside how there are almost exclusively white men here, and the wookiee never gets a medal. </div> </div> </div>I already address this with the last cherry picked screen shot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The OT doesn't bash you over the head with anything. </div> </div> </div>The OT has the narrative subtlety of a brick being thrown through your window. The good guys are good, the bad guys are bad. Luke hero's journey's his way through the story like Campbell wrote the script for Lucas.<br /> <br /> I love it. But it's a campy space opera, not high fucking art. It's intentionally on the nose in its morals, and not shy about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether Mon Mothma is a white man or Palpatine is a black woman is immaterial to their roles in the story. </div> </div> </div>But they're the genders they are because Lucas wanted to push that political agenda at you.<br /> <br /> Oh and sell lots of toys to kids. ESB and RotJ added lots of new background characters and aliens because more toys to sell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the writers had an agenda, it's impossible to tell, because RotJ is still a good story even if you change the characters' genders and races around. </div> </div> </div>No, you just already agree with the OT's agenda so you don't notice it. It's there, and it's blatant as hell. The Jedi of the Light defeat the Sith of the Dark... for someone that cares so much about the symbolism of the number nine... how can you not get the symbolism here?<br /> <br /> Also, the story is schlock. Ewoks with sticks beat a trained army with guns. Palpatine completely forgets that Sith betray each other all the time, and that Vader wants to convert Luke to the Sith (which means Palpatine's gonna have to go....), and turns his back on Vader while torturing Luke because the Emperor needs to go down without Luke striking him down in anger.<br /> <br /> There's a reason ESB is the highest regarded film in the franchise (it actually does some interesting twists with the story between two predictable hero quests), and it's not followed immediately by ANH or RotJ (hint, #2 is from the Disney era).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With characters like Rey? Disney's agenda is very easy to tell, and the character's bad writing and Mary Sue qualities are justified in the name of delivering a strong female character and feminist icon to a modern audience. </div> </div> </div>Ah yes the time honored, &quot;I'm not a sexist, but there's not way my argument make sense unless you accept sexist logic,&quot; approach (sorry, but sexists have ruined the Mary Sue complaint, not that it was ever a good complaint anyway because they took the name of a female character to focus on instead of what was wrong with her as a character, which Rey is nothing like).<br /> <br /> You've been spouted off about how Mon Mothma could have been a Chinese non-binary person and it wouldn't have mattered, but Rey's gender never matters to her whole story. Sure I guess some people would complain about male!Ray and Kylo getting it on, but Rey being a woman has no impact on her story what-so-ever. You know who Larry Kasdan is, yeah? You know he was one of the writers on The Force Awakens? You know what else he co-wrote?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sequels would still be bad movies if Rey's character was made male, so the actual diversity isn't the problem. It's the fact that writers who are most vocal about including greater diversity in stories usually deliver bad stories. </div> </div> </div>The sequels are, despite Internet folks trying to make it sound otherwise, two hits and one divisive move that bombed with critics but did well with audiences (no stinkers like Solo). They're not bad movies, you just don't like them. It's OK not to like things that most people thing are good! Not liking something doesn't have to mean it's bad!<br /> <br /> And JJ Abrams, not Disney, wanted Rey to be female. His reason? Not to craft a feminist icon or any of your theorizing/YouTube binged ideas. He just felt the Star Wars movies had all been focused on a male lead, and wanted to try out a female lead.<br /> <br /> What's so strange to me is Lucas, Abrams, Brucato to get back to the Mage stuff.... none of these people are shy about their motivations. But they're not sitting there going, &quot;this is awesome because diversity!&quot; either like you seem to claim they are. They want to tell stories with diverse characters (even if Lucas reallllllly sucks at that I mean... prequel trilogy... and his attempts to spicy things up was cringy af).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T07:10:10-07:00","id":1463091,"title":"","content":"Leaving star wars Aside because I don't see the point.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't like the Disparate alliance. Largely because the Taftani are one of my favorite factions, and while some of the changes in M20 are good. The vast majority of what made the Taftani awesome was gutted.<br /> <br /> And honestly that kind of seems to be the norm. Much of the unique flavor of these crafts was trimmed away to make them into pale imitations of the Traditions. And that to me just... Kind of sucks.<br /> <br /> Like, to a degree it feels like they wanted to simplify the crafts and bring them together as a 'big alliance' like the Traditions and Technocracy, but a large part of their appeal was their ability to stand on their own, refusing to compromise in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T07:39:00-07:00","id":1463097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463085#post1463085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The context they are presented says the Disparate Alliance exists even in a setting where all metaplot developments are optional. The text outside of the Future Fates sidebars doesn't mention any metaplot. It says the Disparates formed in the '90s, but that it. Nothing about the Avatar Storm, the fall of Doissetep and Horizon, or the Ascension Warrior.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or the Traditions treated the Hollow Ones poorly because they didn't take many of them seriously as mages (<i>&quot;Just rebellious angry Goth kids&quot;</i>), the nine seats on the Council were already filled, and they wanted the Hollow Ones to just join other Traditions rather than stay together as their own. When the Crafts in Revised joined the Council, they became camps in the most similar Traditions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/a/a0/Victory_Celebration_ANH.png/revision/latest?cb=20121227220043\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Leaving aside how there are almost exclusively white men here, and the wookiee never gets a medal...<br /> <br /> The OT doesn't bash you over the head with anything. Whether Mon Mothma is a white man or Palpatine is a black woman is immaterial to their roles in the story. If the writers had an agenda, it's impossible to tell, because RotJ is still a good story even if you change the characters' genders and races around.<br /> <br /> With characters like Rey? Disney's agenda is very easy to tell, and the character's bad writing and Mary Sue qualities are justified in the name of delivering a strong female character and feminist icon to a modern audience.<br /> <br /> The sequels would still be bad movies if Rey's character was made male, so the actual diversity isn't the problem. It's the fact that writers who are most vocal about including greater diversity in stories usually deliver bad stories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How is Rey a Mary Sue? If any thing she works harder than Luke did (he had teachers seeking him out, she had to find hers, his mentor set him up with a ship, she had to steal hers, she fights a half trained apprentice, he blows up the Death Star etc etc) if she is, then James Bond must make your head explode, as must Harry Potter...<br /> <br /> On Topic: House Janissary, the secret police/death squad of the Order of Hermes (who also hit other traditions), flat murders craft members, even if they have joined to keep ideological and paradigm purity, treating them the same way they treat Infernalists/Nephandi. While also leaking information about Mages they don't like to the Union.<br /> <br /> Given that the traditions are AGAIN a military and political union, with secret police, purges, rules etc, why the hell would the crafts join them? <br /> <br /> As to why does the council have 9 seats? Because the OoH demanded that, under threat of war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-08-2021, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T09:39:45-07:00","id":1463107,"title":"","content":"I think the issue from a doyelist perspective is pretty big.<br /> <br /> The DA are just Traditions 2, electric boogaloo.<br /> <br /> It's like if you took VTM, Looked at The Camarilla, Anarchs, and the Sabbat, and then decided that the Anarchs should just be a Camarilla clone but for the other six clans. No wait that might be more interesting because clans are caricatures....<br /> <br /> Most of the Disparates work, from a narrative point of view, because they've got their own thing going and don't want to water down their traditions with globalist bullshit. Because they don't want to share power and cooperate, because they don't want to even pretend that their ultimate arts are somehow comparable to whatever the fuck Merlin or Morgan or Frankenstien are doing. I'd like to think of the Disparates as the Mages on so many steroids they can't integrate with the mainstream. If the Traditions are conservatives, the Disparates are Neo Nazis who're happy to wear the swastika, or the taliban, if the Traditions are progressives, the Disparates work as the blue haired, communist eco-terrorist that has a very warped perception of Marx. Mages are all about Ego, and the Disparates work best to me as the Egos big enough that they don't mix with others. (on a macro organizational level. As Individuals I think they can be good people just like anyone else)<br /> <br /> From another perspective. Everyone else is so global. The Disparates are characterized by... NOT being global. <br /> <br /> Also like... the word Disparate means something. I know most People's republics aren't really for the people, but given <i>The Traditions</i> and <i>The Technocracy</i> holds very true, you'd think <i>The Disparates</i> would too. <br /> <br /> The more i talk, the more I start thinking the Disparate Alliance was the result of someone liking one too many a <i>Jreg</i> video.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-08-2021, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:17:58-07:00","id":1463110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463072#post1463072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Disparates don't really add diversity. Even the most seemingly West-centric Trad are shown to be multicultural.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Disparate don't add diversity, they add self-advocacy, the idea that a minority group don't need a white knight to protect it from the big bad world.<br /> <br /> And the Trad only accept other cultures when those accept to adopt the trappings of their &quot;parent&quot; Trad and the hierarchy of the Council.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463078#post1463078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the point of the Traditions working together is that they don't want to impose their paradigms on the world</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly true, either. It's more that doing so isn't feasible in the foreseeable future, but many of them were fully engaged in trying this when it was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463079#post1463079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because in my experience, the more aggressively authors push a social agenda, the worse their stories and worldbuilding in their settings tends to be. Such authors also tend to disrespect the works of authors that have come before them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every story have a political facet, well written or not. Every author pushes a social agenda of some kind. The only thing you achieve by bashing the agenda instead of the story is to alienate ideas before ever really looking into the story.<br /> <br /> Curiously, you're doing it now with two settings, WoD and SW, that were blatantly political from the beginning and never tried to pretend otherwise. In my experience, &quot;Tainting the franchise with politics&quot; is the go-to argument when you have no other reason to dislike something except your own political agenda, and here it is being directed to an epic about the disenfranchised fighting an over-violent terrorist state and a setting about social criticism and ideological empowerment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463079#post1463079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My &quot;fancy metaphysics&quot; are the axis around which the setting turns.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. By the lore itself this fancy metaphysics is specifically the Order of Hermes magical theory that they imposed over everyone else, with extreme prejudice, and this was a big deal.<br /> <br /> The axis around which the setting turns is that belief shapes magic and will is power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463107#post1463107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The DA are just Traditions 2, electric boogaloo.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a Doylist perspective the DA corrects some of the assumptions of WW in the 1st edition, and this isn't actually a new movement in the setting.<br /> <br /> When 1st edition was made, in a time when WW thought Gipsies was a good idea and respectful depiction, the Traditions were <i>meant</i>, indeed, to be champions of diversity <i><u>as the authors understood it</u></i>.<br /> <br /> But their concept still left a lot of things unrepresented, and the authors picked up this. We started to get a history of the Traditions that explains why they have the structure they have, and we got to see the disgruntled unrepresented factions on the edges, along with equally disgruntled underrepresented factions inside that have joined out of necessity but are far from happy with the arrangement.<br /> <br /> This served the purpose of explaining out the Traditions by casting a not-so-good light on them, saving the setting from having to be rebuilt from scratch, but had the collateral effect of harming the idea that the Traditions really stand for diversity as much as they profess. Not only the Hermetics forced their hand more than once to make it into 9 traditions, keep most seats of power in Europe, force-feed their own Paradigm down everyone's throats (Spheres, 9 Traditions, 4 groups of Magi), but the individual Traditions, being built of not-so-similar groups with only one standing as their representative (because they ARE named after specific &quot;crafts&quot;), ended up repeating the same process down the line as they got to indoctrinate their newcomers.<br /> <br /> Nothing here is a new development, it was taking form as soon as 2nd edition, with seeds already on 1st.<br /> <br /> It only makes sense for the Disparate Alliance to appear. It addresses both Watsonian (those disgruntled Magi would organize sooner or later) and Doylist (players have a group that offers an organized alliance while being even more free on character and Paradigm concept) perspectives.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that saying the Crafts already existed doesn't address the fact that lacking a larger political body to belong to is too limiting a downside in the game as it is. And it is also fun to rub your existence in the face of the OoH beloved tarot analogy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:27:15-07:00","id":1463111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463110#post1463110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly true, either. It's more that doing so isn't feasible in the foreseeable future, but many of them were fully engaged in trying this when it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who? When? Like, the only ones you can maybe argue that for are the Chorus who themselves were always heretical Christians, and indeed they split on exactly that issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:39:00-07:00","id":1463116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463111#post1463111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who? When? Like, the only ones you can maybe argue that for are the Chorus who themselves were always heretical Christians, and indeed they split on exactly that issue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The dark ages setting makes it pretty clear the OoH was big on ruling, as had been the Verbena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T10:42:43-07:00","id":1463117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463110#post1463110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that saying the Crafts already existed doesn't address the fact that lacking a larger political body to belong to is too limiting a downside in the game as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? There's nothing stopping a Taftani from working with a Traditional Cabal. And while that's the group I know best, Hollowers were a pseudo tradition for ages, and the others I feel are similarly able to work with a cabal.<br /> <br /> That's kind of the issue. Instead of being these proud, powerful holdouts who can engage with the Traditions, instead they've been bundled off into their own Ill fitting alliance while losing much of what made them Unique. There's also the question of just what these groups gain by working together with each other, but not the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T11:00:56-07:00","id":1463121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463117#post1463117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How so? There's nothing stopping a Taftani from working with a Traditional Cabal. And while that's the group I know best, Hollowers were a pseudo tradition for ages, and the others I feel are similarly able to work with a cabal.<br /> <br /> That's kind of the issue. Instead of being these proud, powerful holdouts who can engage with the Traditions, instead they've been bundled off into their own Ill fitting alliance while losing much of what made them Unique. There's also the question of just what these groups gain by working together with each other, but not the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Taftani could work with a Traditions cabal, but they couldn't get the larger forces of the Traditions to act for their sake without surrendering a significant degree of autonomy. A single cabal is not an alliance.<br /> <br /> And the point of the Disparate Alliance is, as far as I can tell, that they get to keep being holdouts for the most part. Just now they're holdouts sharing information with other holdouts and working together towards common goals when the opportunities are available. The point of the Disparate Alliance is that they never need to surrender their autonomy to a higher political order, just a general prerogative of sharing information and working together against common enemies. Otherwise, they seem to just keep doing their own thing for the most part. Some groups are more involved with keeping the whole thing working than others, but they aren't giving orders to the individual Crafts. A comparison was made to the Anarchs earlier, and it's actually not a bad one. Just Anarchs with more of a cultural-spiritual thing because, ya know, they're Mages.<br /> <br /> Some groups probably will be more proactive about working as an Alliance, but others can still be part of the club and enjoy some of the benefits without having to make any big promises. It is actually a pretty reasonable move in an increasingly hostile world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T11:15:35-07:00","id":1463125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463079#post1463079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because in my experience, the more aggressively authors push a social agenda, the worse their stories and worldbuilding in their settings tends to be. Such authors also tend to disrespect the works of authors that have come before them.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>I just asked to drop that element of the conversation. Consider this a warning. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T12:46:23-07:00","id":1463133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463088#post1463088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Star Wars stuff]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm splitting this off to a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1463132-debate-the-star-wars-sequels-and-ot\">third thread</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T12:50:58-07:00","id":1463135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463110#post1463110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly true, either. It's more that doing so isn't feasible in the foreseeable future, but many of them were fully engaged in trying this when it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a highly debatable point. Yes, several of the pre-traditions did dominate the cultures of their areas at certain points in history, but they certainly weren't imposing their paradigms in the sense we normally mean in Mage. There was only a short period of time between when the Hermetics started figuring out that reality was mutable and when the Order of Reason grabbed that ball and ran with it, and barely anyone outside of those two groups knew about the possibility until the Council started forming.<br /> <br /> I certainly agree that the OoH of yore might have started a campaign to dominate reality, but it doesn't look like they ever got the chance.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T13:41:23-07:00","id":1463146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463135#post1463135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly agree that the OoH of yore might have started a campaign to dominate reality, but it doesn't look like they ever got the chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's exactly my point. First that many already tried local hegemony before, in whatever scope they could operate by then. Second that the brief period of the OoH grasping the concept of Consensus and not having to deal with the OoR winning, they pretty much tried. Third that the Council is a defensive alliance against the Technocracy, so it isn't that they defend everyone's right, but that they defend everyone helping punch the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Nothing defines the Traditions as universally defending other's right for their Paradigm, their history pre-Council points out to it being unlikely and their internal grudges fully reinforces that even if it is true-ish, many won't extend this right to just everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T14:10:53-07:00","id":1463154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463146#post1463146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's exactly my point. First that many already tried local hegemony before, in whatever scope they could operate by then. Second that the brief period of the OoH grasping the concept of Consensus and not having to deal with the OoR winning, they pretty much tried. Third that the Council is a defensive alliance against the Technocracy, so it isn't that they defend everyone's right, but that they defend everyone helping punch the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Nothing defines the Traditions as universally defending other's right for their Paradigm, their history pre-Council points out to it being unlikely and their internal grudges fully reinforces that even if it is true-ish, many won't extend this right to just everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, it's been 600 years since its founding of mutual cooperation and live and let live. You'd have to be an utter fanatic nutter to think that it was an alliance of conveinance at this point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T14:17:12-07:00","id":1463155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463154#post1463154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, it's been 600 years since its founding of mutual cooperation and live and let live. You'd have to be an utter fanatic nutter to think that it was an alliance of conveinance at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many malcontents in the Trad books. They seem to be a minority, and by this point most probably take the Council for granted, but what would happen in the wake of a definitive victory?<br /> <br /> As it stand, it is just too remote a possibility to say if the alliance would hold or not. Or if they would let the other crafts live after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T14:31:02-07:00","id":1463157,"title":"","content":"Um... *gestures at the whole Sorcerer's Crusade era* there is a distinct period in Mage history where the global Consensus shattered and the world was plunged into a jigsaw of Reality Zones.<br /> <br /> That's when a lot of the regressive parts of the Traditions actually set into their culture because for a few generations of mages, Reality in their home turf was what they believed. Before that magic was just magic, and technology was just technology. Outside of personal magical spaces, a Hermetic's fireball worked the same anywhere on map, and so did gunpowder. During that time, you could cross invisible lines and the rules of Reality changed. On one side of a line praying to Jesus was the best cure for disease, on the other side of the line ancient herbal remedies were, and both were true in their Zones, but false in the other's. This is when the Ascension War became defined as a war over Reality because the Order of Reason was trying to recombine all the Reality Zones into a new one that suited their goals instead of returning it to the old one or letting it stay as is. And at the time, the Traditions wanted things to stay like they were.<br /> <br /> However, once the Order of Reason won and reunified Consensus... the Traditions had to come to grips with the idea they were never getting the Reality Zones for Everyone era back. And thus they started pushing for going farther back: to when the global Consensus was just more flexible accepting of lots of different things. That push is also what kept the strongest Crafts of the day out of the Traditions because they didn't want to accept that solution; they wanted to stay lords of their personal domains (mystically or literally).<br /> <br /> In modern times, the Traditions have spend centuries in the stance of fighting for a new old Reality as epitomized by Horizon. There's a scant handful of mages left that remember the Sorcerer's Crusade era and what it was like to actually have whole countries of Sleepers living under your Reality Zone's rules. It's questionable if anyone is really left from before that (even if some might exist as spirits or Examplars or etc.). Despite the internal fractures in the Traditions, Horizon is dogma that everyone is indoctrinated into. It's part of the identity now and it's far to ingrained to expunge from the faction.<br /> <br /> And that's, ultimately, where their conflict with the Crafts is still rooted: The Crafts don't want Horizon (except the Batini, but they Watsonianly want a Traditions take 2 because they like the idea but they felt the Council was broken from the get go and they're finally trying again). They want everyone to have their own Realm again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T16:51:02-07:00","id":1463175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463121#post1463121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Taftani could work with a Traditions cabal, but they couldn't get the larger forces of the Traditions to act for their sake without surrendering a significant degree of autonomy. A single cabal is not an alliance.<br /> <br /> And the point of the Disparate Alliance is, as far as I can tell, that they get to keep being holdouts for the most part. Just now they're holdouts sharing information with other holdouts and working together towards common goals when the opportunities are available. The point of the Disparate Alliance is that they never need to surrender their autonomy to a higher political order, just a general prerogative of sharing information and working together against common enemies. Otherwise, they seem to just keep doing their own thing for the most part. Some groups are more involved with keeping the whole thing working than others, but they aren't giving orders to the individual Crafts. A comparison was made to the Anarchs earlier, and it's actually not a bad one. Just Anarchs with more of a cultural-spiritual thing because, ya know, they're Mages.<br /> <br /> Some groups probably will be more proactive about working as an Alliance, but others can still be part of the club and enjoy some of the benefits without having to make any big promises. It is actually a pretty reasonable move in an increasingly hostile world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But why would they need to? Pre-M20 the Taftani were <i>utterly wiping the floor </i>with the Technocracy. The middle east was slowly but surely reverting to a Taftani aligned reality zone under their efforts, and the Taftani had been making inroads into America, one of the centers of Technocratic power, since the 1940's.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't know the other crafts to say with as much confidence, but IMO a big part of their draw wasn't that they were 'Stubborn idiots who needed help but wouldn't ask for it.' which is pretty much what M20 portrays them all as.<br /> <br /> When before, the Crafts were utter badasses who could stand on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T17:11:30-07:00","id":1463178,"title":"","content":"Um.... what?<br /> <br /> The Taftani were losing to the Union in any objective view. They claimed being made irrelevant by nobody caring that they ruled over barren wastelands as a victory while the Technocracy actually took over most of their old territory that mattered to mages or Sleepers. Their Reality Zone in the Middle East was explicitly shrinking, not growing.<br /> <br /> And they were stubborn people that needed to adapt, which Revised already sowed the seeds for, and M20 said they finally did.<br /> <br /> The game never presented the Crafts as &quot;utter badasses who could stand on their own,&quot; it presented them as desperate survivors clinging to their pride in not bending the knee to outsiders, facing a world where continued survival without change was unlikely. That's not some change in M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T18:22:11-07:00","id":1463180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463175#post1463175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But why would they need to? Pre-M20 the Taftani were <i>utterly wiping the floor </i>with the Technocracy. The middle east was slowly but surely reverting to a Taftani aligned reality zone under their efforts, and the Taftani had been making inroads into America, one of the centers of Technocratic power, since the 1940's.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't know the other crafts to say with as much confidence, but IMO a big part of their draw wasn't that they were 'Stubborn idiots who needed help but wouldn't ask for it.' which is pretty much what M20 portrays them all as.<br /> <br /> When before, the Crafts were utter badasses who could stand on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not being an expert on this subject, I feel others might respond better to the question of whether or not any individual Craft *needs* the Disparate Alliance. And I'd be inclined to admit that they might get more from the Traditions if they were willing to side with them.<br /> <br /> But again, if it's an arrangement that comes with potential benefits and little to no downsides, why *wouldn't* they? Unlike with the Traditions, the Taftani don't have to accept the authority of some High Council of the Disparates imposing ideas on them or challenging their authority in their territory. Maybe they aren't such fanatical xenophobes that they refuse to talk to or work with the enemies of their enemies? Unless you're trying to argue that the Taftani could take the whole Technocracy in a head-on fight, why *wouldn't* they play ball?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T19:16:19-07:00","id":1463186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463178#post1463178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um.... what?<br /> <br /> The Taftani were losing to the Union in any objective view. They claimed being made irrelevant by nobody caring that they ruled over barren wastelands as a victory while the Technocracy actually took over most of their old territory that mattered to mages or Sleepers. Their Reality Zone in the Middle East was explicitly shrinking, not growing.<br /> <br /> And they were stubborn people that needed to adapt, which Revised already sowed the seeds for, and M20 said they finally did.<br /> <br /> The game never presented the Crafts as &quot;utter badasses who could stand on their own,&quot; it presented them as desperate survivors clinging to their pride in not bending the knee to outsiders, facing a world where continued survival without change was unlikely. That's not some change in M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where on earth you could get that idea?<br /> <br /> They weren't presented as desperate survivors. They were presented as fanatics who were actually winning, at great cost given how many of them were dying, but the metaplot blamed the failures of the US and Soviet Militaries in the middle east on the Taftani kicking the Technocracy out of the area every time they invaded, with warbands of Taftani and their sleeper allies demolishing Technocratic forces, leaving the national militaries mystically unsupported and easy pickings. The metaplot also didn't really paint them as being a 'shrinking' craft, rather the opposite because they were tied to their community. So as the community grew, so did they. Which is how they ended up having a massive presence in Detroit.<br /> <br /> Sure, they establish palaces in remote wastelands. But they were tied to their community as well as the actual geographic region.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463180#post1463180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not being an expert on this subject, I feel others might respond better to the question of whether or not any individual Craft *needs* the Disparate Alliance. And I'd be inclined to admit that they might get more from the Traditions if they were willing to side with them.<br /> <br /> But again, if it's an arrangement that comes with potential benefits and little to no downsides, why *wouldn't* they? Unlike with the Traditions, the Taftani don't have to accept the authority of some High Council of the Disparates imposing ideas on them or challenging their authority in their territory. Maybe they aren't such fanatical xenophobes that they refuse to talk to or work with the enemies of their enemies? Unless you're trying to argue that the Taftani could take the whole Technocracy in a head-on fight, why *wouldn't* they play ball?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were invaded by the Technocracy multiple times over a number of years, and generally speaking kicked their asses every time the Technocrats tried it. The whole meme about Afghanistan being unconquerable was tied to the Taftani being able to repeatedly, consistently, repulse the Technocracy by being more in touch with the local communities and unwilling to hide what they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 10-08-2021, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T19:18:09-07:00","id":1463187,"title":"","content":"The biggest change to the Taftani is that they're not murdering each other as much as they used to.<br /> <br /> Seriously.<br /> <br /> The Taftani cooperate, barely, with outsiders more easily than each other in the past. Taftani that ran into each other that weren't part of a mentor-student relationship dueled to the death. The only way for them to actually work together were to magically arrange neutral meetings where any attendees would be safe from hostilities from each other for seven days (three before, three after) and they only did that twice a year. No longer dueling to the death the moment they come into disagreement with each other, they now try to only start fighting if there's a serious conflict of interest between to of their members.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the Union didn't think it was worth invading their wilderness Reality Zones... they could just take advantage of the Taftani blasting each other into ashes to encroach a bit more every year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T19:25:18-07:00","id":1463188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463186#post1463186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know where on earth you could get that idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting yours?<br /> <br /> This is the Lost Paths discussion of Detroit:<br /> <br /> &quot;In the early part of the twentieth century, right<br /> around 1910, Ford needed labor for his automobile plants<br /> in Detroit. He found it in the Middle East. He brought in<br /> tens of thousands of workers from Yemen, Qatar, Oman,<br /> Syria and a handful of other countries. There were far<br /> more Ahl-i-Batin in that force than Taft\u00e2ni, but some<br /> of us came over too. It opened our eyes to a whole new<br /> continent. Where that goes remains to be seen.&quot;<br /> <br /> Where is the statement of there being a &quot;massive presence&quot; of them there?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T19:32:15-07:00","id":1463189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463187#post1463187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest change to the Taftani is that they're not murdering each other as much as they used to.<br /> <br /> Seriously.<br /> <br /> The Taftani cooperate, barely, with outsiders more easily than each other in the past. Taftani that ran into each other that weren't part of a mentor-student relationship dueled to the death. The only way for them to actually work together were to magically arrange neutral meetings where any attendees would be safe from hostilities from each other for seven days (three before, three after) and they only did that twice a year. No longer dueling to the death the moment they come into disagreement with each other, they now try to only start fighting if there's a serious conflict of interest between to of their members.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the Union didn't think it was worth invading their wilderness Reality Zones... they could just take advantage of the Taftani blasting each other into ashes to encroach a bit more every year.</div> </div> </div> </div>They cooperated in the old lore as well. In fact it was them beginning to cooperate rather than killing each other that allowed them to take Afghanistan from the Technocracy. Which is another thing, their reality zone is only perfect in the Rub Al Khali, yes. But it extended imperfectly over the entirety of Afghanistan. The dominant paradigm in Afghanistan isn't mystical or Technocratic, but Destructive(IE, destructive magick and technocratic procedures are coincidental) thanks to them. And large tracts of it have since turned towards Taftani Mysticism, the main remaining obstacle not being the Technocrats, but the Taliban.<br /> <br /> It was all laid out in Lost Paths. Just like the Taftani following their community over to America when Henry Ford recruited people from the Middle East for his automotive factories.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463188#post1463188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are you getting yours?<br /> <br /> This is the Lost Paths discussion of Detroit:<br /> <br /> &quot;In the early part of the twentieth century, right<br /> around 1910, Ford needed labor for his automobile plants<br /> in Detroit. He found it in the Middle East. He brought in<br /> tens of thousands of workers from Yemen, Qatar, Oman,<br /> Syria and a handful of other countries. There were far<br /> more Ahl-i-Batin in that force than Taft\u00e2ni, but some<br /> of us came over too. It opened our eyes to a whole new<br /> continent. Where that goes remains to be seen.&quot;<br /> <br /> Where is the statement of there being a &quot;massive presence&quot; of them there?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If ever a country has called out to the Taft\u00e2ni, it is<br /> America. Brash, powerful, arrogant \u2014 all of our own<br /> traits we see reflected in the national temperament of that land. While the legendary Black Shaykh may be<br /> able to control his temper and hide his light well enough<br /> to live in New York, there are more Weavers in the<br /> Southwest than anywhere outside the Empty Quarter<br /> and Afghanistan.&quot;<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I mixed that bit up with the Detroit thing. I mainly remembered that they had a massive presence in America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 10-08-2021, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-08T20:08:04-07:00","id":1463190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463189#post1463189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They cooperated in the old lore as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... like... in the face of an active existential threat. That's the mentality that got them to opt into the Disparates. They aren't beating the Technocracy, and the Nephandi threats are getting worse after the large grand unified Taftani war effort to try to purge the Middle East of their foul presence.<br /> <br /> It still remains that the only big change from Rev. to M20 is that the dueling culture has reduced significantly. Which allowed them to cooperate and take over Dubai... which is a much bigger win than Afghanistan in terms of giving the Union a bloody nose. M20 has them pushing the Syndicate out of the control over the Gulf OPEC countries, which is going to let them push the NWO out of some of the Middle East's most influential media companies.<br /> <br /> That's way more success than Afghanistan.<br /> <br /> [quot]And large tracts of it have since turned towards Taftani Mysticism, the main remaining obstacle not being the Technocrats, but the Taliban.[/quote]<br /> <br /> And... that just means the Taftani are yet another group that thought they could take over Afghanistan by stopping someone else from doing that. The Taliban are in charge of Afghanistan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Admittedly, I mixed that bit up with the Detroit thing. I mainly remembered that they had a massive presence in America. </div> </div> </div>There's a very big difference between &quot;a lot for a small Craft&quot; and &quot;massive.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T06:36:02-07:00","id":1463220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463091#post1463091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving star wars Aside because I don't see the point.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't like the Disparate alliance. Largely because the Taftani are one of my favorite factions, and while some of the changes in M20 are good. The vast majority of what made the Taftani awesome was gutted.<br /> <br /> And honestly that kind of seems to be the norm. Much of the unique flavor of these crafts was trimmed away to make them into pale imitations of the Traditions. And that to me just... Kind of sucks.<br /> <br /> Like, to a degree it feels like they wanted to simplify the crafts and bring them together as a 'big alliance' like the Traditions and Technocracy, but a large part of their appeal was their ability to stand on their own, refusing to compromise in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Most of the Disparate groups are all about &quot;Our way or the Highway.&quot; Even the Alibatini, who Heavy Arms reminds us are all about unity, are only about unity on their own terms and no others. These groups were always about their special road or goals. Kopa Leoa (sic), as an example, is about the restoration of the cultures of Polynesia. I'm sure they'd like allies, but they don't see themselves as being in a position to go forth and aide others. The Wu Lung are heirs of a tradition that has sees China as the only real or worthwhile place and the Chinese as the only real and worthy humans, and, unlike the Hermetics, they've never acknowledged a need to change any of their views. They are smoother and more charming than the Hermetics (who isn't) but that doesn't make them better people. It does make them distinctive and interesting. Do we need a Chinese Restaurant reworking of the Hermetics? <br /> <br /> With most of these groups the very things that make them individual and distinctive militates against their being in most alliances. <br /> <br /> This is off topic, but the way arguments on this thread have been going proves to me that we need splatbooks on who these groups are now! All of the groups have been through transformative events in the early 21st century. We need to know who these groups have become. Just look at the Hollow Ones. They lost large numbers of their members. Just about all the Hollowers that respected the Trads have left. The remaining third are Romantic Revolutionaries and require revolutionary change, whether or not a revolution would help or harm. This isn't very Goth. Someone looking to play a Hollow One as described in the early editions of this game is SOL. <br /> <br /> New splatbooks please!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-09-2021, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T08:04:15-07:00","id":1463225,"title":"","content":"What did happen to the pro-Tradition Hollow Ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T08:14:13-07:00","id":1463226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463225#post1463225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did happen to the pro-Tradition Hollow Ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>They mainly entered the Traditions they felt closest too. Or that's what White Wolf or Onyx Path wrote in some place I can't remember now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T08:59:30-07:00","id":1463229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463220#post1463220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With most of these groups the very things that make them individual and distinctive militates against their being in most alliances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have a very limited and unrealistic view of what is both a cultural preservation group and an alliance.<br /> <br /> The Council of Nine Traditions and the Technocratic Union aren't the only models of alliance around. The very idea of the Disparates is that they are an alliance with no interference in each-others affairs. The groups work together in relevant areas and can send some members to meet for specific purposes, but aren't interfering in how each other take care of their own turf. And that's kinda of how most alliances work anyways.<br /> <br /> And groups like them aren't incapable of or unwilling on helping each other. Wanting to keep your own voice is extremely different from being xenophobic, wanting the help of others doesn't mean being incapable of providing any help. Especially since it is an alliance focused on sharing information and assistance, not on sharing other resources necessarily. No one is giving or asking Nodes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T09:29:19-07:00","id":1463233,"title":"","content":"The DA always strikes me as the opportunity to be a part of the founding of the traditions without having to play a historical game, and I suspect that is the main point. It certainly isn\u2019t the inevitable development of the member groups.<br /> <br /> Many of the same elements are there, up to and including a dark secret that could drive everything apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T12:58:46-07:00","id":1463250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463229#post1463229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you have a very limited and unrealistic view of what is both a cultural preservation group and an alliance.<br /> <br /> The Council of Nine Traditions and the Technocratic Union aren't the only models of alliance around. The very idea of the Disparates is that they are an alliance with no interference in each-others affairs. The groups work together in relevant areas and can send some members to meet for specific purposes, but aren't interfering in how each other take care of their own turf. And that's kinda of how most alliances work anyways.<br /> <br /> And groups like them aren't incapable of or unwilling on helping each other. Wanting to keep your own voice is extremely different from being xenophobic, wanting the help of others doesn't mean being incapable of providing any help. Especially since it is an alliance focused on sharing information and assistance, not on sharing other resources necessarily. No one is giving or asking Nodes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume I am limited because I don't agree with you. Having argued with reactionaries ( I don't accuse you of being one) I've been told that a lot. <br /> <br /> Most of these groups have been defined in both their introductions and further expansions as being either isolationist or xenophobic. The Ali Batini have been defined in their last and fullest presentation as cultural imperialists. They need any others they work with to conform to their needs and requirements. The idea that the Hollow Ones or the Ngoma would put up with that is absurd. Then ask how the Bata'a, the Sisters of Hypolita, or Taftani, will deal with it. <br /> <br /> The Sisters of Hypolita see men as spiritually and morally inferior. They also reject the whole idea that Awakened Mages are any different than Sorcerers. A major stumbling block.<br /> <br /> The Taftani want all Mages who aren't part of their order to simply stop. They see all other Mages as having stolen magic from them. <br /> <br /> I get that one can have many different types of organizations. But with half the members rejecting the validity of the others existing, your organizational options are limited. <br /> <br /> Add in that some of the members of the alliance are deeply bigoted, the Templars are religious imperialists, and the Wu Lung are Han supremacists, I have trouble seeing this &quot;organization&quot; lasting a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-10-2021, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T14:31:54-07:00","id":1463254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463225#post1463225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did happen to the pro-Tradition Hollow Ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Traditions accused the Hollowers of being responsible for the Technocratic attack on Horizon, and all the pro-Tradition Hollowers stopped being &quot;pro&quot; after getting tossed under the bus as a group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463250#post1463250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add in that some of the members of the alliance are deeply bigoted, the Templars are religious imperialists, and the Wu Lung are Han supremacists, I have trouble seeing this &quot;organization&quot; lasting a week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides finding the reading of the individual Crafts to continue to rely on a lot of hyperbole (the word xenophobic come up once in all of M20... in the Technocracy section)...<br /> <br /> I've been trying to avoid this historical example, but it seems inevitable and all:<br /> <br /> Japan joined the Axis powers. Why? Because their ideas of how they should run their own countries was close enough that fighting for ultra-nationalist ideology as a group was more important than the fact that their own ideologies said they should all hate each other. The Axis power alliance was essentially built on, &quot;lets crush liberalism first, and then we'll deal with each other.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, yes, humans are completely capable of making these sorts of alliances despite what seems like such an untenable difference. Their dislike of everyone else is something they all have in common... and in common enough that fighting together until everyone else is out of the picture is actually a valid psychological appeal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T16:10:50-07:00","id":1463260,"title":"","content":"A history professor of mine had the alternate view that Hitler was of the &quot;Screw the Rules, I make them&quot; view and declared the Japanese honorary Aryans because he could and it was up to everyone else to get in line. In the end, whatever Nazisms (air quotes) principles (air quotes) were, they bent to his needs.<br /> <br /> Which fits the view the DIsparate Alliance does not need to make sense ideologically if they just want to have more power as a way to keep the other factions at bay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T17:43:19-07:00","id":1463269,"title":"","content":"How Hitler justified it to himself or his people isn't really the issue. Germany was one of many within the military pact. Most of them wanted Japan in because they wanted Japan to help them box in Russia (justifiably, a lot of them ended up Soviet states after WWII) and friends to help fight the communists before the US got in on that was enough for them to put aside any prejudices around Asian peoples and join in with the original three Axis powers. You also have Thailand that joined the Axis (yeah, that's a detail that gets skipped a lot) because Japan wanted to be able to attack British forces in Myanmar/Burma and Thailand was given a choice of invasion or joining up so the Japanese military could move through their land without impediment. It's not like the Thai government at the time liked European colonial powers as neighbors (Japan promised to help Thailand reclaim French colonial territories), and the Japanese were keeping the Chinese from expanding too.<br /> <br /> The point is, as you noted ideology falls to the side of practicality when it comes to these sorts of alliances. Leaders will compromise to defeat external enemies as long as they can sell it well enough to their followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T18:25:51-07:00","id":1463271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463250#post1463250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You assume I am limited because I don't agree with you. Having argued with reactionaries ( I don't accuse you of being one) I've been told that a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I thought you had a limited concept because you didn't seemed to understand my point, which is different from disagreeing. And I fully could be wrong, hence I said that I thought, not that you were.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463260#post1463260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which fits the view the DIsparate Alliance does not need to make sense ideologically if they just want to have more power as a way to keep the other factions at bay.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a more elegant presentation of the point I'm trying to make.<br /> <br /> None of the crafts need to believe in equality. They don't need to have any greater faith or affinity for the others. They need to reach a military agreement and that's all of it.They need to recognize that survival now requires this agreement, and this alone isn't any of them bowing to the ways of any other of them.<br /> <br /> It is pure pragmatism and doesn't need to sacrifice any personal belief. The Ahl-i-Batin can wait for an opportunity to spread the Web of Faith, the Sisters can keep thinking low of men, the Taftani are welcome to keep self-destructing all they like, everyone can keep self-aggrandizing and thinking they're allying to little more than animals and the difference between Magi and Sorcerers is moot.<br /> <br /> Absolutely no one is sharing beliefs or anything. No one is giving up independence, territory, or anything but some time to humor an eventual guest. It is not about being a new organization, is about beating the Technocracy hard and whomever comes their way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T22:09:42-07:00","id":1463282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463271#post1463271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the crafts need to believe in equality. They don't need to have any greater faith or affinity for the others. They need to reach a military agreement and that's all of it.They need to recognize that survival now requires this agreement, and this alone isn't any of them bowing to the ways of any other of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which arguably is what the Traditions already are...<br /> <br /> ...which further exacerbates the issue of the DA's existence of just feeling like &quot;Traditions 2.0&quot; and Brucato trying to slip past being told he can't radically rewrite the Traditions to remove all of their problematic issues, and instead writes another Traditions-esque group.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T22:58:53-07:00","id":1463285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463282#post1463282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which arguably is what the Traditions already are...</div> </div> </div> </div>We beat that horse already in several previous posts. They aren't just this.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are a group with well defined structure and hierarchy, an overarching mystical paradigm about the Nine Seats, and any newcomer must abide to the rules, bow to its hierarchy and adapt to one of the named traditions, because if a craft comes they can't simply occupy the 10th seat, they must butcher their beliefs and structures until they fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T23:11:02-07:00","id":1463286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463285#post1463285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We beat that horse already in several previous posts. They aren't just this.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are a group with well defined structure and hierarchy, an overarching mystical paradigm about the Nine Seats, and any newcomer must abide to the rules, bow to its hierarchy and adapt to one of the named traditions, because if a craft comes they can't simply occupy the 10th seat, they must butcher their beliefs and structures until they fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, is that the case anymore?<br /> <br /> Post-Avatar Storm there's like a dozen masters left and no Horizon Realms so it's now a leveled loose alliance instead of a Pyramid.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T23:20:29-07:00","id":1463289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463285#post1463285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Traditions are a group with well defined structure and hierarchy, an overarching mystical paradigm about the Nine Seats, and any newcomer must abide to the rules, bow to its hierarchy and adapt to one of the named traditions, because if a craft comes they can't simply occupy the 10th seat, they must butcher their beliefs and structures until they fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>...which even pre-Avatar Storm, I have to disagree with, considering a lot of the Traditions don't strike me as the type to abide by such a hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Hermetics, Choristors, and Akashics I could buy doing that. But groups like the Dreamspeakers, Virtual Adepts, and Verbena come across as being a lot looser. And even then, it'd be case-by-case at best.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T23:24:42-07:00","id":1463290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463289#post1463289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...which even pre-Avatar Storm, I have to disagree with, considering a lot of the Traditions don't strike me as the type to abide by such a hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Hermetics, Choristors, and Akashics I could buy doing that. But groups like the Dreamspeakers, Virtual Adepts, and Verbena come across as being a lot looser. And even then, it'd be case-by-case at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the hierarchy exists mostly in theory anyway. A Chantry exists mostly as an island to itself. A Euthanatos, Verbena, Celestial Choirster, and Hermetic may have their own place but none of them are directly answerable to anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T00:14:27-07:00","id":1463292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463286#post1463286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhh, is that the case anymore?<br /> <br /> Post-Avatar Storm there's like a dozen masters left and no Horizon Realms so it's now a leveled loose alliance instead of a Pyramid.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Avatar Storm status is variable in M20. It's an optional setting element now, as is how severe it actually was. Even in the worst case scenario with it, there's already a new Earthly Council of Nine that have reformed the Tradition's overarching hierarchy and enforce it's rules. They're less heavy handed because they lack the pure magical power of their predecessors, but their organizational authority is still rather powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463289#post1463289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...which even pre-Avatar Storm, I have to disagree with, considering a lot of the Traditions don't strike me as the type to abide by such a hierarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they all agree to abide by the hierarchy imposed by the Council. Their looser internal politics don't matter to agreeing to follow the larger organization's rules.<br /> <br /> It's like being a member of the EU. The EU doesn't eliminate all the sovereignty of its member nations, but being an EU member nation comes with a bunch of rules you need to follow for the EU to grant the benefits it offers. The EU, for example, doesn't stop your country from being a constitutional monarchy, a liberal democracy, or (not that any of them actually are) a purely socialist country. But regardless of how a country administers itself, the EU requires certain standards in outcomes.<br /> <br /> As to your three examples<br /> <br /> Half of the potential Dreamspeakers refused to join the Tradition at its founding because they hated the idea (there's a reason there's a lot of Crafts that would fit in with them) and the lack of respect for the diversity of culture outside of Europe.<br /> <br /> The Verbena are absolutely a hierarchy friendly organization. They're more local community focused than many of the others, but social status within their chosen communities is incredibly important to them.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adepts are also obsessed with hierarchy, even if through the lens of subjective communally assign merit rather than other forms. As well, the VAs are the most recent Tradition, that have surviving members that are defectors from the Technocracy. They understand the strength of organization even if they feel the Union's gone too far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463290#post1463290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the hierarchy exists mostly in theory anyway. A Chantry exists mostly as an island to itself. A Euthanatos, Verbena, Celestial Choirster, and Hermetic may have their own place but none of them are directly answerable to anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... no?<br /> <br /> The Council has had an entire Chantry executed before. Chantries are absolutely not islands, even if the Council doesn't have the practical ability to nanny state them (one of the reasons why the Council's actions tended to be extreme is because it can take so long for them to consider bad actors within a Chantry that said mage can easily have gone from a questionable killing to throwing in with the Nephandi or guilt-exploding into a Marauder before they act).<br /> <br /> Like my EU example above, the Council does not dictate how a Chantry organizes itself, but does dictate outcomes. A Chantry's members are answerable to whatever form of leadership they establish for themselves, and that leadership answers to the Council if the rights or duties of any members aren't respected.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T00:37:03-07:00","id":1463293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463292#post1463292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Council has had an entire Chantry executed before. Chantries are absolutely not islands, even if the Council doesn't have the practical ability to nanny state them (one of the reasons why the Council's actions tended to be extreme is because it can take so long for them to consider bad actors within a Chantry that said mage can easily have gone from a questionable killing to throwing in with the Nephandi or guilt-exploding into a Marauder before they act).<br /> <br /> Like my EU example above, the Council does not dictate how a Chantry organizes itself, but does dictate outcomes. A Chantry's members are answerable to whatever form of leadership they establish for themselves, and that leadership answers to the Council if the rights or duties of any members aren't respected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I point to the counterfact that it took literal centuries to note the House of Helekar was living down to every negative stereotype of the Euthanatos and outdoing some Nephandi. There's groups that try to patrol the Traditions for Nephandi, Marauderhood, more general infernalism (Heremetics: *whistle*), and betrayal to the Union but I note that it is a group that does very little top down dictation.<br /> <br /> You're more likely to get a request from a master and strongly encouraged to do it than any idea its like an army. Its an organization that trades in favors, knowledge, and mutual protection.<br /> <br /> At least how the adventures all showed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-10-2021, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T02:24:34-07:00","id":1463296,"title":"","content":"We were talking about the disparate alliance last night post game and the following observation. (Paraphrased)<br /> &quot;I'm not really going to comment on the politics of the disparate alliance. But my main issue is simular to the anarchs in v5 were they're artificially thrust forward without consideration if they're interesting (as a collective, the crafts are all pretty cool) or can carry the setting. Anarchs fundemently cannot following their v5 books failure to just the shift and unless we get a technocracy revised tier magnum opus I don't see the alliance as a workable group over the technocracy for pcs much less the 9.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-10-2021, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T02:27:18-07:00","id":1463297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463296#post1463296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were talking about the disparate alliance last night post game and the following observation. (Paraphrased)<br /> &quot;I'm not really going to comment on the politics of the disparate alliance. But my main issue is simular to the anarchs in v5 were they're artificially thrust forward without consideration if they're not very interesting (as a collective, the crafts are all pretty cool) or can carry the setting. Anarchs fundemently cannot following their v5 book and unless we get a technocracy revised tier magnum opus I don't see the alliance as a workable group over the technocracy for players much less the 9.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Traditions are the Anarchs and the Technocracy is the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> As stated by me in the 90s: &quot;The Matrix is how the Virtual Adepts see the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance is the Independent Clans. I feel like saying they're the Anarchs is a nonstarter when several of them are ten to fifty times more rigidly organized than any Tradition with the Knights Templar and the ax-crazy band of Persian wizards that only exist in their own private circles even if they no longer murder them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T02:39:55-07:00","id":1463298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463297#post1463297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the Traditions are the Anarchs and the Technocracy is the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> As stated by me in the 90s: &quot;The Matrix is how the Virtual Adepts see the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance is the Independent Clans. I feel like saying they're the Anarchs is a nonstarter when several of them are ten to fifty times more rigidly organized than any Tradition with the Knights Templar and the ax-crazy band of Persian wizards that only exist in their own private circles even if they no longer murder them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue they're neither. The institutions are are so different idealogically, logistically and frankly ecologically that any approximate equivalent borders on absurd you may as well compare the Sabbat to the tanarii from d&amp;d simply because both really violent predators . The comparison is more a comment on playability than a in setting blow by blow. The big issue with v5 anarchs is they're criminally underwritten for the emphasis placed on them mage havnt actually hit that issue but it is a potential underlying risk. If the disparate alliance is to become more prominent it needs fleshing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T02:47:16-07:00","id":1463300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463293#post1463293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I point to the counterfact that it took literal centuries to note the House of Helekar was living down to every negative stereotype of the Euthanatos and outdoing some Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not much of a counter when the Ksirafai were explicitly covering up Helekar as one of their many operations meant to undermine the Traditions from within. Helekar was certainly a blight on the Traditions, but they were keeping their activities as secret as they could, and a whole different group was adding more obfuscation to their activities on top of it. That doesn't prove that Chantries are islands, or that the Council doesn't have a command hierarchy... it just means that the Council is a flawed institution (shocking nobody... especially not the Disparates).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're more likely to get a request from a master and strongly encouraged to do it than any idea its like an army. </div> </div> </div>First off, a letter from a master is, if they're even bothering to phrase it as a request, is not something ignored lightly.<br /> <br /> Second, who said anything about it working like an army? The Council has some militaristic natures to its apparatuses, but only because they're an institution created to wage war on the Technocracy. That doesn't mean the Council operates like a military. It operates like the UN (including the ability to have members commit their military resources to the common cause), but is actually more functional than the UN because they're not trying to include everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T03:08:08-07:00","id":1463301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463296#post1463296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were talking about the disparate alliance last night post game and the following observation. (Paraphrased)<br /> &quot;I'm not really going to comment on the politics of the disparate alliance. But my main issue is simular to the anarchs in v5 were they're artificially thrust forward without consideration if they're interesting (as a collective, the crafts are all pretty cool) or can carry the setting. Anarchs fundemently cannot following their v5 books failure to just the shift and unless we get a technocracy revised tier magnum opus I don't see the alliance as a workable group over the technocracy for pcs much less the 9.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Is the Disparate Alliance interesting?&quot; is ultimately subjective. I find them interesting, clearly others don't. The big thing for me is that I find the WoD's default to having two main warring factions with some side minor factions for flavor rather boring. Adding factions, even if in this case just one, lets you tell more varied stories.<br /> <br /> &quot;Can the setting?&quot; I honestly don't know what this means exactly. Can you run a Disparate Alliance game where all the PCs are members of it? Then sure. I don't buy the idea that they need something like Guide to the Technocracy here. GttTech, like GttSabbat, had to work hard to make factions that were largely defined by being violently antagonistic to the default PCs and make them compelling as protagonists. The Disparate Alliance is taking groups that were already compelling protagonists - even if limited in what sort of stories you could tell with them - and having them work together instead of staying separate. It's an entirely different development lift.<br /> <br /> And the Disparates are supposed to be a tenuous organization that might crash and burn before it gets anything significant done. M20 core already both acknowledges that and puts it forward as one of the main reasons to play them over the others: taking a long shot at trying something different in the hopes of getting better results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463297#post1463297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the Traditions are the Anarchs and the Technocracy is the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beside how poor of a fit VtM factions to MtA factions are...<br /> <br /> The Traditions and the Technocracy are both Camarillas fighting to be the last one standing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As stated by me in the 90s: &quot;The Matrix is how the Virtual Adepts see the world.&quot; </div> </div> </div>While not a horrible elevator pitch, it really isn't true beyond a very surface layer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Disparate Alliance is the Independent Clans. </div> </div> </div>If you want to fairly compare them to anyone, they're not the Independent Clans, they're the Hecata without the Capuchin keeping everyone in line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T07:30:43-07:00","id":1463308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463301#post1463301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Is the Disparate Alliance interesting?&quot; is ultimately subjective. I find them interesting, clearly others don't. The big thing for me is that I find the WoD's default to having two main warring factions with some side minor factions for flavor rather boring. Adding factions, even if in this case just one, lets you tell more varied stories.<br /> <br /> &quot;Can the setting?&quot; I honestly don't know what this means exactly. Can you run a Disparate Alliance game where all the PCs are members of it? Then sure. I don't buy the idea that they need something like Guide to the Technocracy here. GttTech, like GttSabbat, had to work hard to make factions that were largely defined by being violently antagonistic to the default PCs and make them compelling as protagonists. The Disparate Alliance is taking groups that were already compelling protagonists - even if limited in what sort of stories you could tell with them - and having them work together instead of staying separate. It's an entirely different development lift.<br /> <br /> And the Disparates are supposed to be a tenuous organization that might crash and burn before it gets anything significant done. M20 core already both acknowledges that and puts it forward as one of the main reasons to play them over the others: taking a long shot at trying something different in the hopes of getting better results.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certianly true but I can draw a rough concensus (lol) on if they are in fact genrally considered interesting, I've yet to encounter anyone IRL who has any enthusiasm for the group. Individuals Crafts certainly but as a collective group pretty much all feedback has been negative. Now this is obviously a limited perspective but without a deeper feedback study I'm forced to conclude they're not considered particulary interesting in my personal experiance, Especially considering I myself find them collectively uniteresting. Personally I've always considered the ascention war a 3 way struggle disguised as a two way one incidently.<br /> <br /> carry the setting as in be a viable long term progonist for the game and I'm unconvinced they can pull that off. I can theorectically run a Nephandi game so theoretically yes. I can run a Alliance game, the issue isnt can I? it's should I? i'll conceed the individual groups have potential but as a collective it's a bit of a big meh.<br /> <br /> I'm not really convinced they really are that differant at least to the 9 mt's, they're effectuvely very simular to the 9 mt's but more genrally ethno centric and less infrastructure. I'm told this sect is distinct from the 9 and the union but I'm really not seeing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-10-2021, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T08:00:45-07:00","id":1463313,"title":"","content":"Personally I think the DA is a good idea, but agree that they may benefit from a proper book on them. Not necessarily a <i>magnum opus</i>, but something to explore the group.<br /> <br /> They are interesting already due to their members, which isn't something to be ignored. I don't think it so hard to figure out goals and conflicts among the Crafts that make them up. But I do agree that this isn't a lot for someone who isn't already interested on the Crafts. A pitch for the group is missing.<br /> <br /> Either way that isn't the only thing to make them a good or valid setting element. The Neffandi and Marauders aren't meant for a lot of play as protagonists, but are interesting setting elements by themselves for use as NPCs, background, ominous threats or many other roles. The DA likewise expands the ST's arsenal of tools in any chronicle as they put more weight and mobility on the crafts, making them a viable player in the Great Game the Traditions and Technocracy were trying to play alone.<br /> <br /> Also, by their mere presence they can pressure the other two to adapt. They can't look at any given Craft as only a local threat anymore, they need to come to grips with a more organized third faction. There is no correct answer, but they can't just choose to not answer and expect for this to have no consequences.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the end I'm totally for a new book exploring the DA and updating the Crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T08:10:58-07:00","id":1463315,"title":"","content":"The Disparates certainly want, and could reasonably be said to need, more power. That's true Montparnasse. The problem is that the Disparates are presented as being a vibrant new force. &quot;New Force&quot; I can see that. &quot;Vibrant?&quot; That's what I find wildly unlikely.<br /> <br /> I've had coursework on African history taught by a man ( Dr. Andrew Clark) who spoke more than a dozen African languages fluently. He did oral history in Africa recording the Girots and similar figures. <br /> <br /> The simple fact of most African nations is that if they pulled together against their common problems they could be strong and build prosperity. Ancient animosities overwhelm practically time and again. Europe only got by their ancient bitterness with each other by first being ground to dust by WWII and then facing the threat of the U.S.S.R. And then it was a long hard slog towards any unity. And Brexit has shown how quick people are over there to toss the benefits of unity away.<br /> <br /> The Disparates as a weak association occasionally trading intelligence and resources makes sense. That's something that could fit in the setting. But as a new force equal to the Trads or the Technos, that's just not viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T08:37:52-07:00","id":1463320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463315#post1463315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Disparates as a weak association occasionally trading intelligence and resources makes sense. That's something that could fit in the setting. But as a new force equal to the Trads or the Technos, that's just not viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if they need to be more than a loose association to become a strong contender, given how complex this interplay can be. It isn't about being as militarily strong or as wealth, but about being just organized enough to not be ignored. They still have fairly distinct goals.<br /> <br /> And they're not as a rule groups ridden with ancient animosity. Many of them barely interacted in the past. There is a big difference there. Regions like Afghanistan or most of Africa are divided between local groups that fought among themselves for ages, but precisely because they're near each other and locked in local conflicts. But the DA works as an information network and support group for people that only share that common enemy. They share global interests while keeping their local matters untouched.<br /> <br /> Not to say that conflicts will never arise. And you can make the DA implode at your table due to one or more of them. But those dynamics do not play the same way all the time. Some may learn to keep working together because they ARE under that much pressure for survival. Others may learn a way to keep those conflicts from getting in the way of the Alliance as a whole. Things may get ugly, yet the DA survive. It may get tainted as it is corrupted by the conflicts, or it may get stronger as it adapts to them.<br /> <br /> There are many others forms of alliances the world around than the infighting among tribes in Africa after the careful European work in creating the worse bedfellows possible there. Even the situation in Africa is far more complex and nuanced than simply say they can't work together, even if this is true. Many variables are different to determine what will be the outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T10:46:22-07:00","id":1463327,"title":"","content":"Brexit is also a hard example to point to because the UK didn't go completely isolationist... they took themselves out of one of a multitude of international multi-party organizations they belong to. The UK itself is still holding together despite being four countries with a long history of hating each other violently. Plus the amount of buyer's remorse that's already starting to set in even if rejoining the EU isn't likely to happen soon is nothing to overlook. Instead of the rest of the EU questioning the strength of their choice to remain together after the UK left (which there was worry about), the UK is pretty much a poster child for, &quot;leaving the EU is an incredibly dumb idea.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mage, for good reasons, doesn't have the layers upon layers of geopolitics to capture that dynamic. Well, you could in theory, do a bit as some of the cross-Tradition factions might appeal to working with some of the Disparate Alliance, but it wouldn't be anything like the UK being in NATO while leaving the EU.<br /> <br /> Of course, pointing at Europe in general and talking about both war and an external enemy grinding away differences to allow greater unity... how is that not the history of the Disparates? The Ascension War, which most of them wanted no part in, has cost them countless members and forced many of them to recede to the edges of societies they were once prominent members of, robbing them of mundane and magical resources. The Nephandi are directly painted as their main external antagonist, as they see the Traditions vs. the Technocracy as a complete distraction from the spreading power of the Fallen. So those two elements are strongly present in the game. If massive devastating war + major external threat = good chance of unity despite long histories of division... then history would be on the Disparate's side, not against it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463308#post1463308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really convinced they really are that differant at least to the 9 mt's, they're effectuvely very simular to the 9 mt's but more genrally ethno centric and less infrastructure. I'm told this sect is distinct from the 9 and the union but I'm really not seeing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This why I said earlier that the DA is rather dependent on the metaplot to make sense. If this was a brand new game without &quot;20&quot; years of history and metaplot behind it, I would agree with this sentiment.<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance is, absolutely, in the same place as the Council was when it started... but the Council has centuries of history, and some very major recent history, that have shaped it into something very different from how it started.<br /> <br /> To point to the above talk about the UK... that's kind of what the Traditions have become. Sure, in the UK, being Scottish and being Welsh are very important cultural differences, and sometimes enough that tensions about keeping the United part of the nation's name seems questionable. But they've stayed together for centuries and have a joint national identity as citizens of the UK.<br /> <br /> What I feel like distracts from the differences between the Traditions and the Disparates is that they're all mystic mages (even with the SoE and VAs around), in a game so heavily defined by the Traditions mysticism vs. Technocratic super-science. A potential new second faction of mystic mages looks redundant from that perspective.<br /> <br /> But from a political and philosophic standpoint, putting aside the trappings of how willworkers do their art, a centuries old political union that honors its individual member groups in culture more than political reality is extremely different from a highly organized state with internal divisions determined by the needs of the state, and just as different from a mutual collective cooperative alliance of independent nations.<br /> <br /> To change up my real world analogs a bit, saying that the Council and the Alliance seem to similar is like saying you don't see a difference between the USA as a federal republic of fifty sovereign states, and the EU as a parliamentary alliance of twenty seven sovereign nations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-10-2021, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T19:47:21-07:00","id":1463363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463065#post1463065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solificati coroner who helps investigate/cover up weird goings on, Ahl-i-Batin arbitrator called in to keep the crafts/Traditions from clashing to badly, Knight Templar: basically Michael Carpenter from the Dresden Files, call then in to apply large amounts of holy beat stick, and as moral guide who legit is trying to live the nicer parts of the new testament. Sisters of Hippolyta 'transporter' works for an underground railroad, helping people awakened or not, escape war zones, drug wars, etc</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463070#post1463070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hollower information broker that specializes in knowledge of other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> A cross-Craft cabal of a Templar, Taftani, and a Batini working to help clean up the utter supernatural mess that is the canon state of Cairo while preserving Egypt's diverse culture in the post-Arab Spring environment.<br /> <br /> A Wu Lung investment banker that's using the Belt and Road Initiative to take control over land in east Africa (of the ideas off the top of my head this one is the easiest to do as ally or rival)<br /> <br /> A Sister of Hippolyta that goes into abusive homes to get women and children out and to shelters even if it risks pissing off physically dangerous or well connected people that could bring trouble to other mages by association.<br /> <br /> The Kopa Loei that keeps asking Pele to ruin road construction to protect sacred lands, but has been getting to blatant about it and it's starting to get unwelcome attention on all levels... from the new curse highway tourist craze, to the Technocrats getting tired of their projects being behind schedule.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463033#post1463033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are three questions that could help any storyteller in planning to include the Disparate Alliance:<br /> <br /> 1) Given a vast geographic area, like Africa, that the Disparate Alliance is supposed to be dominant in, what fun possibilities can you you explore that are pertinent to that part of the world?<br /> <br /> 2) Can you imagine <i>A Single NPC</i> who is from one of the Crafts belonging to the Disparate Alliance that you would enjoy running in your Chronicle? Looking at it this way takes some of the pressure off that would come with calculating the politics of a DA Cabal.<br /> <br /> 3) Is there a Plot that you can run with this NPC that would not be possible with the other factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>#1: Toward the goal of building a green economy, developing countries have an advantage over those that were decades ahead in the building of grey-economy real estate. Suppose you wanted to construct a high tech building that has a negative electricity cost, grows food and has homes and offices inside. When choosing where to build, you would prefer not to have to buy expensive land with an existing building that has to be demolished. New green energy projects are also easier where there is totally undeveloped land. If modernizing and decarbonizing are something everyone will have to do to avoid extinction, it is developing countries who can do this with more freedom in terms of available land space. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QX3M8Ka9vUA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QX3M8Ka9vUA</a><br /> <br /> #2: My favorite from each of the replies above (considering the concept of building green):<br /> - Ahl-i-Batin arbitrator called in to keep the crafts/Traditions from clashing to badly<br /> - A Wu Lung investment banker that's using the Belt and Road Initiative to take control over land in east Africa<br /> - My first edition to the group would be Claver Nimubona, a Gnoma engineer and geomancer from Burundi. His Paradigm is Turning the Keys to Reality. He is an optimist in a land where hope is scarce. He is interested in combining vertical agriculture with drone transport to diversify the crops produced there and increase yield. Being on the equator, Burundi has abundant sun that would allow solar-powered drone aircraft to transport seed and other materials from vertical farm buildings with specialized landing balconies.<br /> <br /> #3: The Wu Lung wants to own what he's investing in and is holding all the cards to begin with. Claver has asked the Ahl-i-Batin to look for Tradition partners with money to invest who could offer competitive terms... Nice open ended tie-in for a Tradition Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T06:00:39-07:00","id":1463416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463320#post1463320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if they need to be more than a loose association to become a strong contender, given how complex this interplay can be. It isn't about being as militarily strong or as wealth, but about being just organized enough to not be ignored. They still have fairly distinct goals.<br /> <br /> And they're not as a rule groups ridden with ancient animosity. Many of them barely interacted in the past. There is a big difference there. Regions like Afghanistan or most of Africa are divided between local groups that fought among themselves for ages, but precisely because they're near each other and locked in local conflicts. But the DA works as an information network and support group for people that only share that common enemy. They share global interests while keeping their local matters untouched.<br /> <br /> Not to say that conflicts will never arise. And you can make the DA implode at your table due to one or more of them. But those dynamics do not play the same way all the time. Some may learn to keep working together because they ARE under that much pressure for survival. Others may learn a way to keep those conflicts from getting in the way of the Alliance as a whole. Things may get ugly, yet the DA survive. It may get tainted as it is corrupted by the conflicts, or it may get stronger as it adapts to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably one of the places I would put my focus if I were running a Disparate game. The alliance is based on an idealistic view that they can work with each other without too much compromise or contamination. I might even say it is naive, but I don't mean that in the sense that it is wrong but in the sense that it is untested. The game, then, would be about testing it with unanticipated problems and seeing how the characters defend it or push it to adapt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T12:54:41-07:00","id":1463454,"title":"","content":"I haven't had a chance to read the thread so far (RL has been taking up an inordinate amount of my time), so this may have already been addressed; but: <br /> <br /> The idea that the mage factions slot neatly into the Stasis/Dynamism/Entropy triad is a relic of earlier editions. It is something that Brucato has been attempting to downplay almost from the moment that he took over as line developer. I know that MRev stated that the traditions represent questing while the technocracy represents pattern, the Marauders represent dynamism, and the Nephandi represents the primordial; but I think I could make an equally good claim for the Disparates representing primordialism: they are, after all, primarily composed of factions that preserve the old way of doing things. Certainly, they represent \u201cthe Primordial\u201d at least as well as the Nephandi do. <br /> <br /> And frankly, I wouldn't be inclined to have the Marauders or the Nephandi \u201crepresent\u201d specific Avatar Essences; I'd be more inclined to go with a seven-slot structure (the four Essences, plus the three legs of the Metaphysical Trinity); and the flaw wouldn't be that there's nowhere to put the Disparates, but rather that there are two slots unfilled: the Traditions, Technocracy, and Disparates would fill the Questing, Pattern, and Primordial Essence slots, whole the Marauders and Nephandi would fill the Dynamism and Entropy Metaphysical slots; that would leave the Dynamic Essence slot and the Stasis Metaphysical slots unfilled. <br /> <br /> But I wouldn't actually do <i>that</i>, either. I like M20's notion of a more diverse and individualistic culture for mages as a whole, with all of the elements I described above being present in every faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T14:48:28-07:00","id":1463471,"title":"","content":"There are a number of positions one could have with regard to the claim of the OP title.<br /> <br /> 1. The DA is a bad setting element and I don't use them for that reason.<br /> 2. The DA is a bad setting element, but I use them, since they are the default NPC faction in large parts of the world (PCs can take Corr3, so they are good to know about).<br /> 3. The DA is a good setting element, but I don't use them or haven't had the chance.<br /> 4. The DA is a good setting element that I use and my Chronicle is better for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T14:55:16-07:00","id":1463473,"title":"","content":"My position is that the DA is an OK setting element that I may or may not use, depending on the needs of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-11-2021, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T15:04:19-07:00","id":1463475,"title":"","content":"I definitely find the Craft groups more interesting without an alliance - the decision to remain completely independent and not recognize the authority of any group outside their own being exactly what defined them as distinct as a pseudo-non-faction-faction from the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T15:38:16-07:00","id":1463480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463473#post1463473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My position is that the DA is an OK setting element that I may or may not use, depending on the new of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they are useful alternative to the Nephandi as a third Earthly faction with rational motivations (as opposed to nihilism). A power triangle has a lot more room for roleplaying and dialogue than a two-faction grudge match. So far, my story is set in North America. I am pondering some DA or unaffiliated Craft NPCs to bring into the story. <br /> <br /> I will probably have an unaffiliated Craft character play a cameo role just to throw them off, giving them the impression that Crafts are niche loners. Then I can develop and unfold a DA plot that suits the setting. A DA Mage makes contact with the PCs, inviting them to visit some island paradise. After, either the same or another DA character posing as a Tradition Mystic attacks a Technomancer with dementing Magick, breaking the truce in the regional setting. If the players escape the conflict by accepting the invitation to the island paradise, they are slowly pumped for information about the Traditions back home.<br /> <br /> I also have an idea for a Technocratic Union campaign, where PCs would investigate a location previously occupied by DA Mages. It may be a long while before I can use that one, but I will write, just for fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T20:12:01-07:00","id":1463528,"title":"","content":"My disagreement with many criticisms of the Disparate Alliance stems from a difference of value judgements.<br /> <br /> Opponents of DA point to the ways in which the Crafts are different, and conclude that it cannot work. That these are irreconcilable differences, and thus the game shouldn't try to put them together.<br /> <br /> Conversely, I see these differences as storytelling <span style=\"color:#FFD700\"><i>GOLD</i></span>. It provides so many opportunities for conflicts, setbacks, mysteries, and challenges. Players have the chance to MAKE the alliance work, or to see it all come crashing down around them. The potential incompatibility with the various members's ideologies, attitudes, and goals is not a bug. It's a <i>feature</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't know if such an alliance could work out. But it would be very interesting to watch. Better yet, to play out in a game.<br /> <br /> Any attempts to appeal to reasons why it wouldn't work is, to me, all the more reason to do it. The absolute worst thing you could do for a roleplaying game is present an interesting scenario, and have it succeed or fail &quot;off screen&quot;, with no input from the players or Storytellers. Because that's boring and squanders opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T14:09:52-07:00","id":1463746,"title":"","content":"I think that everyone has pretty much provided all the compelling arguments against and in favor of the Disparate Alliance, so instead I'm going to provide my interpretation and let people use it, or not, as they see fit.<br /> <br /> First off, why it's so hard to imagine that groups with, pardon the pun, disparate beliefs would band together if the incentive is powerful enough? Like, let's say, avoid extinction? Let's see the position that the crafts find themselves if you follow most of the metaplot. A progrom by the technocracy, ignored or absorbed by the traditions, and the avatar storm that killed their leadership and horizon bases...all that with the added pressure of a society that has exploited, killed, slander, and pushed them to the fringe's year after year, and none of the crafts had even half the resources of the technocracy or the traditions to weather it. Taking that into account, from my point of view, the disparate alliance wasn't really a choice, but the only logical option they had to survive the attacks and influence of more powerful organizations of mages that wanted to destroy or absorb them, and also pushing back against a global paradigm that wanted to make them irrelevant.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm willing to concede that even in such abysmal conditions, it's possible that some crafts would remain so stubborn as to just remain isolated even if it meant destruction. That's when you introduce what I consider the deciding factor in my head cannon, the intervention of the Ahl-i-Batin. The subtle ones saw the rising power and influence of the nephandi, something had to be done, but they judged the technocracy too corrupted to save and the Council of Nine as a complete failure. The crafts provided an opportunity for something new, a council 2.0 if you will, or perhaps they just needed pawns to use against the nephandi. In any case, through diplomacy and subterfuge, they pushed the idea of the alliance and the need to fight the real threat: the nephandi. With that, they gave the crafts an idea of how to reach to each other and a cause to rally around.<br /> <br /> So, for me as of now, the disparate alliance is a defensive alliance focused on sharing intel and assistance to guarantee survival against a paternalistic council of nine and destroy the allegedly nephandi takeover of the Technocracy. Beyond that? Whether the alliance will work is something that, from my point of view, is meant to <b>be</b> <b>explored in the game. </b>They are a storyteller resource to enrich the experience, first and foremost. All the back and forward arguments discussed here are rich with role-playing potential, these are the kind of conflicts that I would very much like to explore in a campaign. The crafts could rise as the third power ready to challenge the other two, or they can collapse in spectacular fashion, or maybe they could even help broke peace in the ascension war. Their fate is ours to decide at our tables, and I intend to use them to try to make a more interesting campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 10-25-2021, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T14:37:31-07:00","id":1463886,"title":"","content":"The best summation of this thread I can think of is we need two more books in the Mage20 line. A) a book of the Disparates that would both describe where these crafts are now and how they both work and fail to work together. The twenty to twenty-five years between these crafts being written down and where the crafts are now is supposed to be a period of massive change. Tell us what the changes were. And B) a book of crafts covering groups we've been told about for years but got few details on and a chapter, and a solid one, on making your own crafts.<br /> <br /> By the way. The group that needs an update/new explanation the most is the Hollow Ones. The difference between the 90s Hollow Ones and the present group reminds me of an old Val Lewton film, The Seventh Victim. The two women in the final scenes sum up the Hollow Ones for me. The woman who is dying of an unknown disease but decides to just go out and live the life she still has reminds me of the 90s Hollow Ones. They felt they were doomed but they weren't willing to just give up without a party. The modern Hollow Ones are like the other woman in the scene. She decides to just kill herself because the struggle to live would require effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 10-15-2021, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T15:07:01-07:00","id":1463888,"title":"","content":"Yeah; no. That's not the modern Hollow Ones. Mages are too willful to have an entire Craft that's suicidal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T15:52:31-07:00","id":1463896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463888#post1463888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; no. That's not the modern Hollow Ones. Mages are too willful to have an entire Craft that's suicidal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more the perversity and pigheadedness of that film character I was evoking. The perky Goths with teeth (90's Hollow Ones) are more fun than the self-righteous prudes with an attitude (present day Hollow Ones).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T06:02:37-07:00","id":1464728,"title":"","content":"Anyway, my own view of the difference between the Traditions and the Disparates is that the former believe that Magick is ultimately just Willworking, and that Practices are window dressing that ultimately are to be discarded; as a rule, the Disparates don't. <i>They're</i> the setting's advocates for \u201cFocus matters\u201d \u2014 the ones who say that you shouldn't have to compromise your principles or identity to get along with others, and that Practices are important in and of themselves. They view the Traditions as a sort of mystical \u201cTechnocracy lite\u201d: more benign than the Union, but still dedicated to the goal of assimilation into a unified whole. The idea that the Traditions and the Disparates are not meaningfully distinguishable is actually a Technocratic perspective \u2014 more due to its focus on conformity which contrasts with both factions' comparative diversity. And meanwhile, the Traditions see the Union and the Disparates as both attaching too much importance to Practice, with themselves being the only ones who have realized that it's something to be overcome, not relied on. <br /> <br /> And in all of these cases, I'm describing their various ideals. In practice, none of them live up to their ideals: the Technocracy isn't as unified as it claims to be; the Traditions don't always live up to their vision of transcending their Practices; and the Disparates have learned that \u201cnever compromise\u201d, followed too rigidly, is a good way to die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-22-2021, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T08:13:13-07:00","id":1464738,"title":"","content":"A few additional thoughts: <br /> <br /> \u2022 the Ahl-i-Batin and Hollow Ones, as noted, are exceptions within the Disparate Alliance: the former because Unity is their goal, and they're the driving force behind the \u201cAlliance\u201d part of the Disparate Alliance; and the latter because they <i>have</i> accepted the notion that Practice is just window dressing, and ultimately meaningless. But in the former case, the Batini are trying for a different kind of Unity this time around, one that respects and preserves the disparate views of their allies; and in the latter case, the meaninglessness of Practice is just a part of their larger philosophy that it's <i>all</i> ultimately meaningless, in the end. <br /> <br /> \u2022 This view of the Disparate Alliance also informs my view of Navalon, which as I see it was conceived in M20 to eventually be the Disparate Alliance's technomantic faction. As such, I'd prefer their overall worldview to be more akin to the above description of the Disparate Alliance than to the way the Technocracy or Traditions work. Unlike the Society of Ether and the Mercurial Elite, Navalon hasn't bought into the notion that Science is ultimately just a flavor of Magick; but unlike the Union, Navalon doesn't seek to impose its will on others: it prefers to \u201clead by example\u201d, <i>showing</i> that its approach to Science is superior and letting others convert or not as they will instead of conditioning people to toe the party line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-22-2021, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T15:08:44-07:00","id":1464795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1463069#post1463069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point of order but in the OG star wars movie, the rebels looked like this<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://starwarz.com/tbone/wp-content/uploads/2011/08/85.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> That's a lot of white human males. Alongside a single black man I think they get two alien pilots in <i>The Empire Strikes Back</i>. All those aliens, as Obi Wan puts it, belong in a &quot;Hive of Scum and Villainy&quot;. GL might've made a good point of female leaders, but there's not much else there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many episodes of both Doctor Who and The Prisoner were written to have wide ethnic and racial diversity. The demographics of the British acting pool in period cancelled a worthy effort. Just adding a Black Woman and an Asian Man to the regular cast caused sixties Star Trek to look more like America than any other TV show for a decade. <br /> <br /> We need to make distinctions between places that could have been far more inclusive (Hollywood, Britain after the mid-Seventies ) and those places that simply lack an ethnically and racially diverse acting pool. <br /> <br /> That said, making an effort to let people know that diverse casts are a necessity helps encourage the maximum available diversity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T15:18:53-07:00","id":1464797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1464728#post1464728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, my own view of the difference between the Traditions and the Disparates is that the former believe that Magick is ultimately just Willworking, and that Practices are window dressing that ultimately are to be discarded; as a rule, the Disparates don't. <i>They're</i> the setting's advocates for \u201cFocus matters\u201d \u2014 the ones who say that you shouldn't have to compromise your principles or identity to get along with others, and that Practices are important in and of themselves. They are the Traditions as a sort of mystical \u201cTechnocracy lite\u201d: more benign than the Union, but still dedicated to the goal of assimilation into a unified whole. The idea that the Traditions and the Disparates are not meaningfully distinguishable is actually a Technocratic perspective \u2014 more due to its focus on conformity which contrasts with both factions' comparative diversity. And meanwhile, the Traditions see the Union and the Disparates as both attaching too much importance to Practice, with themselves being the only ones who have realized that it's something to be relied on not overcome.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That turns the classic Hollow Ones upsidedown. The Hollow Ones used to mock the Order of Hermes for caring about foci and study. Remember, the present day Hollow Ones are supposed to be Romantic Revolutionaries. (For Right and Romance!). Your suggestion flips the Hollow Ones and the Order of Hermes totally around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T00:23:16-07:00","id":1464832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463010-the-disparate-alliance-is-a-bad-setting-element?p=1464797#post1464797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That turns the classic Hollow Ones upsidedown. The Hollow Ones used to mock the Order of Hermes for caring about foci and study. Remember, the present day Hollow Ones are supposed to be Romantic Revolutionaries. (For Right and Romance!). Your suggestion flips the Hollow Ones and the Order of Hermes totally around.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> It's probably not the best idea to make too broad and sweeping statements about beliefs, especially when it comes to the Disparates. Their whole angle is that they're a bunch of disparate groups, united by circumstance and certain shared goals (undermining the Technocracy, rooting out Nephandi, etc). Saying that they are ALL &quot;this, that, and the other thing&quot; is contrary to that.<br /> <br /> Plus, while many groups have mostly done their own thing and avoided entanglements with Tradition mages, that doesn't mean they're ignorant. They've all, at one time or another, been pitched to join the Traditions (either at its founding or later), if only as a subordinate group to the Nine. They aren't unfamiliar with the concept of Willworking, even if they prefer to believe otherwise. Some, whether whole Crafts or just members within, may accept Willworking or at least acknowledge it might be possible.<br /> <br /> Then there are the Ahl-i-Batin, who used to be a Tradition, and the Hollow Ones, who tried to be for years. More than any other, I think they'd be down with the idea of Willworking. They care more about what you do with the magick than about some purity of ideology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:17:10-07:00","id":1464844,"title":"","content":"Umm\u2026 isn't that what I just said?<br /> <br /> First, I never said that they're \u201cALL \u2018this, that, or the other thing\u2019\u201d. Second, I never claimed that they're ignorant. Third, I specifically addressed the Batini and the Hollowers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-22-2021, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T21:41:47-07:00","id":1464966,"title":"","content":"Notable fact: I have never played a Tradition mage. Only Unionists and Hollow Ones.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.am